/* Topic 2 integration, separate from approved Topic 1 and Topic 3 code. */
const topic2Lecture=[{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"Topic 2: Evaluating and Selecting Quality Literature"},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"主题二：评估与选择优质儿童文学作品 Zhǔtí èr: Pínggū yǔ xuǎnzé yōuzhì értóng wénxué zuòpǐn"},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"Introduction"},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"引言 Yǐnyán"},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"Children need books that are enjoyable, meaningful, beautiful, and suitable for their stage of development. 儿童需要有趣、有意义、富有美感并适合其发展阶段的书籍。 Értóng xūyào yǒuqù, yǒu yìyì, fùyǒu měigǎn bìng shìhé qí fāzhǎn jiēduàn de shūjí."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"Choosing a good book is more than choosing a colourful cover or a popular story. 选择一本好书，不只是挑选封面鲜艳或广受欢迎的故事。 Xuǎnzé yì běn hǎo shū, bù zhǐ shì tiāoxuǎn fēngmiàn xiānyàn huò guǎng shòu huānyíng de gùshi."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"Teachers need to consider the story, illustrations, book design, language, cultural representation, and children's individual needs. 教师需要考虑故事内容、插图、书籍设计、语言、文化呈现以及儿童的个别需求。 Jiàoshī xūyào kǎolǜ gùshi nèiróng, chātú, shūjí shèjì, yǔyán, wénhuà chéngxiàn yǐjí értóng de gèbié xūqiú."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"A high-quality book can invite children to think, imagine, feel, ask questions, and discover new ideas. 优质的书籍能够引导儿童思考、想象、感受、提问并发现新想法。 Yōuzhì de shūjí nénggòu yǐndǎo értóng sīkǎo, xiǎngxiàng, gǎnshòu, tíwèn bìng fāxiàn xīn xiǎngfǎ."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"This topic helps teachers learn how to evaluate books and select literature that supports young children's learning and enjoyment. 本主题帮助教师学习如何评估书籍，并选择能够支持幼儿学习与阅读乐趣的文学作品。 Běn zhǔtí bāngzhù jiàoshī xuéxí rúhé pínggū shūjí, bìng xuǎnzé nénggòu zhīchí yòu'ér xuéxí yǔ yuèdú lèqù de wénxué zuòpǐn."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"Learning Outcomes"},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"学习成果 Xuéxí chéngguǒ"},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"By the end of this topic, students should be able to: 完成本主题后，学生应该能够： Wánchéng běn zhǔtí hòu, xuéshēng yīnggāi nénggòu:"},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"1. Identify the main features of high-quality picture books. 识别优质图画书的主要特点。 Shíbié yōuzhì túhuàshū de zhǔyào tèdiǎn."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"2. Explain how format, layout, typography, and illustrations affect the reading experience. 解释书籍形式、版面设计、字体排版和插图如何影响阅读体验。 Jiěshì shūjí xíngshì, bǎnmiàn shèjì, zìtǐ páibǎn hé chātú rúhé yǐngxiǎng yuèdú tǐyàn."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"3. Select books that suit children's ages, abilities, interests, languages, and experiences. 选择适合儿童年龄、能力、兴趣、语言和生活经验的书籍。 Xuǎnzé shìhé értóng niánlíng, nénglì, xìngqù, yǔyán hé shēnghuó jīngyàn de shūjí."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"2.1 Criteria for Evaluating Picture Books: Literary Quality and Artistic Merit"},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"2.1 评估图画书的标准：文学品质与艺术价值 2.1 Pínggū túhuàshū de biāozhǔn: wénxué pǐnzhì yǔ yìshù jiàzhí"},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"What makes a picture book high quality?"},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"什么样的图画书才是优质的？ Shénme yàng de túhuàshū cái shì yōuzhì de?"},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"A picture book tells a story or shares information through words, pictures, or both. 图画书通过文字、图画或两者结合来讲述故事或传递信息。 Túhuàshū tōngguò wénzì, túhuà huò liǎngzhě jiéhé lái jiǎngshù gùshi huò chuándì xìnxī."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"In a good picture book, the words and pictures work together to create meaning. 在优秀的图画书中，文字和图画相互配合，共同表达意义。 Zài yōuxiù de túhuàshū zhōng, wénzì hé túhuà xiānghù pèihé, gòngtóng biǎodá yìyì."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"A book does not need complicated words to be of high quality. 一本书不需要使用复杂的词语，也可以成为优质作品。 Yì běn shū bù xūyào shǐyòng fùzá de cíyǔ, yě kěyǐ chéngwéi yōuzhì zuòpǐn."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"Simple language can express deep feelings, interesting ideas, and memorable experiences. 简单的语言也能表达深刻的情感、有趣的想法和令人难忘的经历。 Jiǎndān de yǔyán yě néng biǎodá shēnkè de qínggǎn, yǒuqù de xiǎngfǎ hé lìng rén nánwàng de jīnglì."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"Teachers can evaluate a picture book by looking at its literary quality, artistic merit, emotional impact, and suitability for its readers. 教师可以从文学品质、艺术价值、情感影响以及读者适宜性等方面评估图画书。 Jiàoshī kěyǐ cóng wénxué pǐnzhì, yìshù jiàzhí, qínggǎn yǐngxiǎng yǐjí dúzhě shìyíxìng děng fāngmiàn pínggū túhuàshū."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"Literary quality"},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"文学品质 Wénxué pǐnzhì"},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"Literary quality refers to how well a story uses language, characters, events, and ideas to engage readers. 文学品质是指故事如何运用语言、人物、事件和想法来吸引读者。 Wénxué pǐnzhì shì zhǐ gùshi rúhé yùnyòng yǔyán, rénwù, shìjiàn hé xiǎngfǎ lái xīyǐn dúzhě."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"1. An engaging story 1. 引人入胜的故事 1. Yǐnrén rùshèng de gùshi"},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"A good story gives children a reason to keep listening or turning the pages. 好故事能让儿童想继续聆听或翻阅下一页。 Hǎo gùshi néng ràng értóng xiǎng jìxù língtīng huò fānyuè xià yí yè."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"The story may include a problem, a surprise, a journey, a funny event, or an interesting discovery. 故事可以包含一个问题、一个惊喜、一段旅程、一件有趣的事情或一次有意思的发现。 Gùshi kěyǐ bāohán yí ge wèntí, yí ge jīngxǐ, yí duàn lǚchéng, yí jiàn yǒuqù de shìqing huò yí cì yǒuyìsi de fāxiàn."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"The events should usually connect in a way that children can follow. 故事中的事件通常应该彼此连贯，让儿童能够理解。 Gùshi zhōng de shìjiàn tōngcháng yīnggāi bǐcǐ liánguàn, ràng értóng nénggòu lǐjiě."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"For example, a child who loses a favourite toy may search for it, ask for help, and discover a new way to solve the problem. 例如，一个孩子丢失了心爱的玩具，可能会四处寻找、请求帮助，并发现解决问题的新方法。 Lìrú, yí ge háizi diūshī le xīn'ài de wánjù, kěnéng huì sìchù xúnzhǎo, qǐngqiú bāngzhù, bìng fāxiàn jiějué wèntí de xīn fāngfǎ."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"2. Believable and interesting characters 2. 可信而有趣的人物 2. Kěxìn ér yǒuqù de rénwù"},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"Characters can be children, adults, animals, imaginary creatures, or other figures. 人物可以是儿童、成人、动物、想象中的生物或其他角色。 Rénwù kěyǐ shì értóng, chéngrén, dòngwù, xiǎngxiàng zhōng de shēngwù huò qítā juésè."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"Children often enjoy characters who have feelings, make choices, face challenges, and learn from experiences. 儿童通常喜欢会感受情绪、作出选择、面对挑战并从经历中学习的人物。 Értóng tōngcháng xǐhuan huì gǎnshòu qíngxù, zuòchū xuǎnzé, miànduì tiǎozhàn bìng cóng jīnglì zhōng xuéxí de rénwù."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"Characters do not need to be perfect to be meaningful. 人物不必完美，也可以具有深刻的意义。 Rénwù bù bì wánměi, yě kěyǐ jùyǒu shēnkè de yìyì."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"A character who feels jealous, makes a mistake, or struggles to make friends can help children discuss real-life experiences. 一个会嫉妒、会犯错或难以交朋友的人物，可以帮助儿童讨论真实生活中的经历。 Yí ge huì jídù, huì fàncuò huò nányǐ jiāo péngyou de rénwù, kěyǐ bāngzhù értóng tǎolùn zhēnshí shēnghuó zhōng de jīnglì."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"3. Language and storytelling 3. 语言与叙事 3. Yǔyán yǔ xùshì"},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"Good children's literature uses language that fits its intended readers while still offering opportunities to learn. 优秀的儿童文学会使用适合目标读者的语言，同时提供学习机会。 Yōuxiù de értóng wénxué huì shǐyòng shìhé mùbiāo dúzhě de yǔyán, tóngshí tígōng xuéxí jīhuì."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"Repetition, rhythm, rhyme, sound effects, and carefully chosen words can make a story enjoyable. 重复、节奏、押韵、声音效果和精心选择的词语，都能让故事更有趣。 Chóngfù, jiézòu, yāyùn, shēngyīn xiàoguǒ hé jīngxīn xuǎnzé de cíyǔ, dōu néng ràng gùshi gèng yǒuqù."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"A story can introduce new words without making every sentence difficult. 故事可以介绍新词语，而不必让每个句子都变得难懂。 Gùshi kěyǐ jièshào xīn cíyǔ, ér bù bì ràng měi ge jùzi dōu biànde nándǒng."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"For example, repeated phrases in a predictable story allow children to join in and build confidence. 例如，可预测故事中的重复句子能让儿童一起参与，并增强自信。 Lìrú, kě yùcè gùshi zhōng de chóngfù jùzi néng ràng értóng yìqǐ cānyù, bìng zēngqiáng zìxìn."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"4. A meaningful ending 4. 有意义的结尾 4. Yǒu yìyì de jiéwěi"},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"An ending should connect with the story and give children something to think or feel about. 结尾应该与故事相呼应，并带给儿童值得思考或感受的内容。 Jiéwěi yīnggāi yǔ gùshi xiāng hūyìng, bìng dài gěi értóng zhídé sīkǎo huò gǎnshòu de nèiróng."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"The ending may solve the main problem, show a change in a character, or leave space for discussion. 结尾可以解决主要问题、展现人物的变化，或留出讨论的空间。 Jiéwěi kěyǐ jiějué zhǔyào wèntí, zhǎnxiàn rénwù de biànhuà, huò liú chū tǎolùn de kōngjiān."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"Not every story needs a perfectly happy ending. 并不是每个故事都需要一个完全快乐的结局。 Bìng bú shì měi ge gùshi dōu xūyào yí ge wánquán kuàilè de jiéjú."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"A thoughtful ending can help children discuss disappointment, change, hope, or different points of view. 引人思考的结尾可以帮助儿童讨论失望、变化、希望或不同的观点。 Yǐnrén sīkǎo de jiéwěi kěyǐ bāngzhù értóng tǎolùn shīwàng, biànhuà, xīwàng huò bùtóng de guāndiǎn."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"Artistic merit"},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"艺术价值 Yìshù jiàzhí"},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"Artistic merit refers to the quality and effectiveness of the illustrations and other visual features. 艺术价值是指插图及其他视觉元素的品质与表现效果。 Yìshù jiàzhí shì zhǐ chātú jí qítā shìjué yuánsù de pǐnzhì yǔ biǎoxiàn xiàoguǒ."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"Illustrations are not simply decorations added to make a book look attractive. 插图并不只是为了让书籍更漂亮而添加的装饰。 Chātú bìng bú zhǐ shì wèile ràng shūjí gèng piàoliang ér tiānjiā de zhuāngshì."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"They can show feelings, provide clues, create atmosphere, and communicate information that the words do not explain. 插图可以表现情绪、提供线索、营造气氛，并传达文字没有说明的信息。 Chātú kěyǐ biǎoxiàn qíngxù, tígōng xiànsuǒ, yíngzào qìfēn, bìng chuándá wénzì méiyǒu shuōmíng de xìnxī."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"1. Use of colour 1. 色彩的运用 1. Sècǎi de yùnyòng"},{"type":"image","figure":1,"src":"assets/topic2_figure_1.png","alt":"Topic 2 illustration, Figure 1"},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"Figure 1 — Colour and mood / 图一：色彩与气氛 / Tú yī: Sècǎi yǔ qìfēn"},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"Warm colours — Cool colours\n暖色——冷色\nNuǎnsè — Lěngsè"},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"Energy — Calm\n活力——平静\nHuólì — Píngjìng"},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"Colours can help create a mood or draw attention to important details. 色彩可以营造气氛，或吸引读者注意重要的细节。 Sècǎi kěyǐ yíngzào qìfēn, huò xīyǐn dúzhě zhùyì zhòngyào de xìjié."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"Warm colours may create a feeling of energy, while cooler colours may create a calm atmosphere, depending on how the artist uses them. 暖色可能营造活力感，而冷色可能营造平静的气氛，具体取决于艺术家的运用方式。 Nuǎnsè kěnéng yíngzào huólì gǎn, ér lěngsè kěnéng yíngzào píngjìng de qìfēn, jùtǐ qǔjué yú yìshùjiā de yùnyòng fāngshì."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"There is no single colour rule that applies to every book. 并没有一种适用于所有书籍的固定色彩规则。 Bìng méiyǒu yì zhǒng shìyòng yú suǒyǒu shūjí de gùdìng sècǎi guīzé."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"2. Line, shape, and texture 2. 线条、形状与质感 2. Xiàntiáo, xíngzhuàng yǔ zhìgǎn"},{"type":"image","figure":2,"src":"assets/topic2_figure_2.png","alt":"Topic 2 illustration, Figure 2"},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"Figure 2 — Lines, shapes and textures / 图二：线条、形状与质感 / Tú èr: Xiàntiáo, xíngzhuàng yǔ zhìgǎn"},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"Soft lines — Sharp lines\n柔和的线条——尖锐的线条\nRóuhé de xiàntiáo — Jiānruì de xiàntiáo"},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"Circle — Square — Triangle\n圆形——正方形——三角形\nYuánxíng — Zhèngfāngxíng — Sānjiǎoxíng"},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"Artists use lines, shapes, and textures to create characters, settings, movement, and feelings. 艺术家运用线条、形状和质感来塑造人物、场景、动作和情感。 Yìshùjiā yùnyòng xiàntiáo, xíngzhuàng hé zhìgǎn lái sùzào rénwù, chǎngjǐng, dòngzuò hé qínggǎn."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"Soft lines may create a gentle feeling, while sharp or uneven lines may suggest tension or excitement. 柔和的线条可能营造温柔的感觉，而尖锐或不规则的线条可能表现紧张或兴奋。 Róuhé de xiàntiáo kěnéng yíngzào wēnróu de gǎnjué, ér jiānruì huò bù guīzé de xiàntiáo kěnéng biǎoxiàn jǐnzhāng huò xīngfèn."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"Different materials, such as paint, collage, pencil, or digital drawing, can create different visual effects. 不同的材料，例如颜料、拼贴、铅笔或数码绘画，可以产生不同的视觉效果。 Bùtóng de cáiliào, lìrú yánliào, pīntiē, qiānbǐ huò shùmǎ huìhuà, kěyǐ chǎnshēng bùtóng de shìjué xiàoguǒ."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"3. Composition and visual focus 3. 构图与视觉焦点 3. Gòutú yǔ shìjué jiāodiǎn"},{"type":"image","figure":3,"src":"assets/topic2_figure_3.png","alt":"Topic 2 illustration, Figure 3"},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"Figure 3 — Illustration techniques / 图三：插画技法 / Tú sān: Chāhuà jìfǎ"},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"Watercolour — Collage\n水彩画——拼贴画\nShuǐcǎihuà — Pīntiēhuà"},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"Pencil drawing — Digital illustration\n铅笔画——数码插画\nQiānbǐhuà — Shùmǎ chāhuà"},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"Composition refers to how people, objects, and spaces are arranged in an illustration. 构图是指插图中人物、物体和空间的安排方式。 Gòutú shì zhǐ chātú zhōng rénwù, wùtǐ hé kōngjiān de ānpái fāngshì."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"A clear visual focus helps children notice important parts of the picture. 清晰的视觉焦点能帮助儿童注意图画中的重要部分。 Qīngxī de shìjué jiāodiǎn néng bāngzhù értóng zhùyì túhuà zhōng de zhòngyào bùfen."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"Sometimes, a small object hidden in a busy picture gives children a reason to look carefully and discuss what they notice. 有时，隐藏在复杂图画中的小物件，会引导儿童仔细观察并讨论自己的发现。 Yǒushí, yǐncáng zài fùzá túhuà zhōng de xiǎo wùjiàn, huì yǐndǎo értóng zǐxì guānchá bìng tǎolùn zìjǐ de fāxiàn."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"4. Consistency and purpose 4. 一致性与表现目的 4. Yízhìxìng yǔ biǎoxiàn mùdì"},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"The illustrations should support the book's purpose and help readers understand or experience the story. 插图应该支持书籍的目的，并帮助读者理解或体验故事。 Chātú yīnggāi zhīchí shūjí de mùdì, bìng bāngzhù dúzhě lǐjiě huò tǐyàn gùshi."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"An unusual or playful art style can be excellent when it suits the story. 如果独特或富有趣味的艺术风格适合故事，它也可以非常出色。 Rúguǒ dútè huò fùyǒu qùwèi de yìshù fēnggé shìhé gùshi, tā yě kěyǐ fēicháng chūsè."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"Teachers should not assume that realistic drawings are always better than imaginative or abstract illustrations. 教师不应该认为写实的图画总是比富有想象力或抽象的插图更好。 Jiàoshī bù yīnggāi rènwéi xiěshí de túhuà zǒng shì bǐ fùyǒu xiǎngxiànglì huò chōuxiàng de chātú gèng hǎo."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"Emotional impact and reader engagement"},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"情感影响与读者参与 Qínggǎn yǐngxiǎng yǔ dúzhě cānyù"},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"A quality book gives children opportunities to feel curious, amused, surprised, comforted, or thoughtful. 优质书籍能让儿童感到好奇、愉快、惊讶、安心或有所思考。 Yōuzhì shūjí néng ràng értóng gǎndào hàoqí, yúkuài, jīngyà, ānxīn huò yǒusuǒ sīkǎo."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"Children may connect a character's experience with their own lives. 儿童可能会把人物的经历与自己的生活联系起来。 Értóng kěnéng huì bǎ rénwù de jīnglì yǔ zìjǐ de shēnghuó liánxì qǐlái."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"For example, a story about starting preschool may help a child talk about feeling nervous, making friends, or missing family members. 例如，关于开始上幼儿园的故事，可以帮助儿童谈论紧张、交朋友或想念家人的感受。 Lìrú, guānyú kāishǐ shàng yòu'éryuán de gùshi, kěyǐ bāngzhù értóng tánlùn jǐnzhāng, jiāo péngyou huò xiǎngniàn jiārén de gǎnshòu."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"Teachers should allow different responses instead of expecting every child to feel the same way. 教师应该允许儿童有不同的反应，而不是要求每个孩子都有相同的感受。 Jiàoshī yīnggāi yǔnxǔ értóng yǒu bùtóng de fǎnyìng, ér bú shì yāoqiú měi ge háizi dōu yǒu xiāngtóng de gǎnshòu."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"Representation, culture, and inclusion"},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"文化呈现与包容性 Wénhuà chéngxiàn yǔ bāoróngxìng"},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"Good books show people and experiences with care, respect, and variety. 优秀的书籍会以细心、尊重和多样化的方式呈现人物与生活经验。 Yōuxiù de shūjí huì yǐ xìxīn, zūnzhòng hé duōyànghuà de fāngshì chéngxiàn rénwù yǔ shēnghuó jīngyàn."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"Children should have opportunities to see different families, languages, cultures, abilities, and ways of living. 儿童应该有机会看到不同的家庭、语言、文化、能力和生活方式。 Értóng yīnggāi yǒu jīhuì kàndào bùtóng de jiātíng, yǔyán, wénhuà, nénglì hé shēnghuó fāngshì."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"In Malaysia, books may include Malay, Chinese, Indian, Orang Asli, Sabah, and Sarawak experiences without suggesting that every community is the same. 在马来西亚，书籍可以呈现马来族、华族、印度族、原住民、沙巴和砂拉越的生活经验，同时避免暗示每个群体都完全相同。 Zài Mǎláixīyà, shūjí kěyǐ chéngxiàn Mǎláizú, Huázú, Yìndùzú, yuánzhùmín, Shābā hé Shālāyuè de shēnghuó jīngyàn, tóngshí bìmiǎn ànshì měi ge qúntǐ dōu wánquán xiāngtóng."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"A stereotype shows a group in an overly simple or unfair way. 刻板印象会以过度简单或不公平的方式呈现某个群体。 Kèbǎn yìnxiàng huì yǐ guòdù jiǎndān huò bù gōngpíng de fāngshì chéngxiàn mǒu ge qúntǐ."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"For example, a book should not suggest that all boys dislike caring activities or that all girls dislike building things. 例如，书籍不应该暗示所有男孩都不喜欢照顾他人的活动，或所有女孩都不喜欢搭建东西。 Lìrú, shūjí bù yīnggāi ànshì suǒyǒu nánhái dōu bù xǐhuan zhàogù tārén de huódòng, huò suǒyǒu nǚhái dōu bù xǐhuan dājiàn dōngxi."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"Inclusive books can show children with disabilities participating, making choices, developing friendships, and contributing to their communities. 包容性的书籍可以呈现残障儿童参与活动、作出选择、建立友谊并为社区作出贡献的情景。 Bāoróngxìng de shūjí kěyǐ chéngxiàn cánzhàng értóng cānyù huódòng, zuòchū xuǎnzé, jiànlì yǒuyì bìng wèi shèqū zuòchū gòngxiàn de qíngjǐng."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"Teachers should consider whether a book represents people respectfully and gives characters meaningful roles. 教师应该考虑书籍是否尊重地呈现不同的人，并赋予人物有意义的角色。 Jiàoshī yīnggāi kǎolǜ shūjí shìfǒu zūnzhòng de chéngxiàn bùtóng de rén, bìng fùyǔ rénwù yǒu yìyì de juésè."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"Accuracy and purpose"},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"准确性与目的 Zhǔnquèxìng yǔ mùdì"},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"Information books should present facts accurately and clearly. 知识类图书应该准确、清楚地呈现事实。 Zhīshi lèi túshū yīnggāi zhǔnquè, qīngchu de chéngxiàn shìshí."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"A story based on history, culture, science, or real events should be checked for misleading information. 以历史、文化、科学或真实事件为基础的故事，应该检查是否包含误导性信息。 Yǐ lìshǐ, wénhuà, kēxué huò zhēnshí shìjiàn wéi jīchǔ de gùshi, yīnggāi jiǎnchá shìfǒu bāohán wùdǎoxìng xìnxī."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"Fantasy stories may include imaginary creatures and impossible events, but they should still make sense within their own story world. 幻想故事可以包含虚构生物和不可能发生的事件，但这些内容仍应符合故事本身的世界设定。 Huànxiǎng gùshi kěyǐ bāohán xūgòu shēngwù hé bù kěnéng fāshēng de shìjiàn, dàn zhèxiē nèiróng réng yīng fúhé gùshi běnshēn de shìjiè shèdìng."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"Teachers should also consider the book's purpose, such as entertaining, informing, inviting discussion, or supporting a particular learning experience. 教师也应该考虑书籍的目的，例如娱乐、提供信息、引发讨论或支持特定的学习体验。 Jiàoshī yě yīnggāi kǎolǜ shūjí de mùdì, lìrú yúlè, tígōng xìnxī, yǐnfā tǎolùn huò zhīchí tèdìng de xuéxí tǐyàn."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"Practical activity: The picture-book detective"},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"实践活动：图画书小侦探 Shíjiàn huódòng: Túhuàshū xiǎo zhēntàn"},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"Choose a picture book and examine it like a detective. 选择一本图画书，像侦探一样仔细检查。 Xuǎnzé yì běn túhuàshū, xiàng zhēntàn yíyàng zǐxì jiǎnchá."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"Look at the story, characters, language, illustrations, cultural representation, and ending. 观察故事、人物、语言、插图、文化呈现和结尾。 Guānchá gùshi, rénwù, yǔyán, chātú, wénhuà chéngxiàn hé jiéwěi."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"Ask whether the book gives children something interesting to think about, feel, or discuss. 思考这本书是否提供有趣的内容，让儿童思考、感受或讨论。 Sīkǎo zhè běn shū shìfǒu tígōng yǒuqù de nèiróng, ràng értóng sīkǎo, gǎnshòu huò tǎolùn."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"Identify one strength and one possible concern. 找出一个优点和一个可能需要注意的问题。 Zhǎochū yí ge yōudiǎn hé yí ge kěnéng xūyào zhùyì de wèntí."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"Explain whether you would choose this book for your class and give your reasons. 说明你是否会为班级选择这本书，并解释原因。 Shuōmíng nǐ shìfǒu huì wèi bānjí xuǎnzé zhè běn shū, bìng jiěshì yuányīn."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"2.2 Concepts of Design: Format, Layout, Typography, and Integration of Text and Image"},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"2.2 设计概念：书籍形式、版面设计、字体排版以及文字与图像的结合 2.2 Shèjì gàiniàn: shūjí xíngshì, bǎnmiàn shèjì, zìtǐ páibǎn yǐjí wénzì yǔ túxiàng de jiéhé"},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"Book format"},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"书籍形式 Shūjí xíngshì"},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"Book format refers to the physical or digital form of a book and the way it is made. 书籍形式是指书籍的实体或数码形态，以及它的制作方式。 Shūjí xíngshì shì zhǐ shūjí de shítǐ huò shùmǎ xíngtài, yǐjí tā de zhìzuò fāngshì."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"Different formats offer different experiences for young children. 不同的书籍形式会为幼儿带来不同的阅读体验。 Bùtóng de shūjí xíngshì huì wèi yòu'ér dàilái bùtóng de yuèdú tǐyàn."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"Board books 硬纸板书 Yìngzhǐbǎn shū"},{"type":"image","figure":4,"src":"assets/topic2_figure_4.png","alt":"Topic 2 illustration, Figure 4"},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"Figure 4 — Comparing book formats / 图四：比较书籍形式 / Tú sì: Bǐjiào shūjí xíngshì"},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"Board book — Thick pages\n硬纸板书——厚书页\nYìngzhǐbǎn shū — Hòu shūyè"},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"Picture book — Wordless picture book\n图画书——无字图画书\nTúhuàshū — Wúzì túhuàshū"},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"Board books have thick pages that are easier for many babies and toddlers to handle. 硬纸板书的页面较厚，许多婴儿和幼儿更容易拿取和翻阅。 Yìngzhǐbǎn shū de yèmiàn jiào hòu, xǔduō yīng'ér hé yòu'ér gèng róngyì náqǔ hé fānyuè."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"They often include simple pictures, familiar objects, and short labels or phrases. 这类书通常包含简单的图画、熟悉的物品以及简短的名称或短语。 Zhè lèi shū tōngcháng bāohán jiǎndān de túhuà, shúxī de wùpǐn yǐjí jiǎnduǎn de míngchēng huò duǎnyǔ."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"Picture books 图画书 Túhuàshū"},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"Picture books use illustrations and words together to tell a story or share information. 图画书结合插图与文字来讲述故事或传递信息。 Túhuàshū jiéhé chātú yǔ wénzì lái jiǎngshù gùshi huò chuándì xìnxī."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"They may use full-page pictures, short text, or detailed scenes for children to explore. 它们可以使用整页图画、简短文字或供儿童探索的细致场景。 Tāmen kěyǐ shǐyòng zhěng yè túhuà, jiǎnduǎn wénzì huò gōng értóng tànsuǒ de xìzhì chǎngjǐng."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"Wordless picture books 无字图画书 Wúzì túhuàshū"},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"Wordless picture books tell stories mainly through illustrations. 无字图画书主要通过插图来讲述故事。 Wúzì túhuàshū zhǔyào tōngguò chātú lái jiǎngshù gùshi."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"Children can describe the pictures, invent dialogue, predict events, and create their own versions of the story. 儿童可以描述图画、创作对话、预测事件，并编出自己的故事版本。 Értóng kěyǐ miáoshù túhuà, chuàngzuò duìhuà, yùcè shìjiàn, bìng biān chū zìjǐ de gùshi bǎnběn."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"These books can support children who communicate in different ways or are learning the language of the text. 这类书可以支持使用不同沟通方式的儿童，也适合正在学习书中语言的儿童。 Zhè lèi shū kěyǐ zhīchí shǐyòng bùtóng gōutōng fāngshì de értóng, yě shìhé zhèngzài xuéxí shū zhōng yǔyán de értóng."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"Pop-up, lift-the-flap, and interactive books 立体书、翻翻书与互动书 Lìtǐshū, fānfānshū yǔ hùdòngshū"},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"These formats may invite children to lift, move, discover, or explore parts of a page. 这些形式可能邀请儿童掀开、移动、发现或探索页面的不同部分。 Zhèxiē xíngshì kěnéng yāoqǐng értóng xiānkāi, yídòng, fāxiàn huò tànsuǒ yèmiàn de bùtóng bùfen."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"Teachers should check that moving parts are safe, durable, and suitable for the children's ages and abilities. 教师应该检查活动部件是否安全、耐用，并适合儿童的年龄与能力。 Jiàoshī yīnggāi jiǎnchá huódòng bùjiàn shìfǒu ānquán, nàiyòng, bìng shìhé értóng de niánlíng yǔ nénglì."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"Digital books 数码书籍 Shùmǎ shūjí"},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"Digital books may include narration, sound, animation, or touch-based activities. 数码书籍可能包含旁白、声音、动画或触控活动。 Shùmǎ shūjí kěnéng bāohán pángbái, shēngyīn, dònghuà huò chùkòng huódòng."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"Useful digital features should support the story rather than distract children from it. 有用的数码功能应该支持故事，而不是分散儿童对故事的注意力。 Yǒuyòng de shùmǎ gōngnéng yīnggāi zhīchí gùshi, ér bú shì fēnsàn értóng duì gùshi de zhùyìlì."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"Teachers should consider screen time, sound levels, accessibility, advertisements, privacy, and opportunities for adult-child interaction. 教师应该考虑屏幕使用时间、音量、无障碍功能、广告、隐私以及成人与儿童互动的机会。 Jiàoshī yīnggāi kǎolǜ píngmù shǐyòng shíjiān, yīnliàng, wú zhàng'ài gōngnéng, guǎnggào, yǐnsī yǐjí chéngrén yǔ értóng hùdòng de jīhuì."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"The best format depends on the purpose of the book and the needs of the child. 最合适的书籍形式取决于书籍的目的和儿童的需求。 Zuì héshì de shūjí xíngshì qǔjué yú shūjí de mùdì hé értóng de xūqiú."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"Layout and page design"},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"版面与页面设计 Bǎnmiàn yǔ yèmiàn shèjì"},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"Layout refers to how words, pictures, and empty spaces are arranged on a page or across two facing pages. 版面设计是指文字、图画和留白如何安排在单页或相对的两页上。 Bǎnmiàn shèjì shì zhǐ wénzì, túhuà hé liúbái rúhé ānpái zài dān yè huò xiāngduì de liǎng yè shàng."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"A clear layout helps children know where to look and how to follow the story. 清晰的版面能帮助儿童知道该看哪里，以及如何跟随故事发展。 Qīngxī de bǎnmiàn néng bāngzhù értóng zhīdào gāi kàn nǎlǐ, yǐjí rúhé gēnsuí gùshi fāzhǎn."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"White space 留白 Liúbái"},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"White space is the empty space around text and illustrations. 留白是文字和插图周围没有被内容占据的空间。 Liúbái shì wénzì hé chātú zhōuwéi méiyǒu bèi nèiróng zhànjù de kōngjiān."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"It can make a page easier to read and help important details stand out. 留白可以让页面更容易阅读，并突出重要细节。 Liúbái kěyǐ ràng yèmiàn gèng róngyì yuèdú, bìng tūchū zhòngyào xìjié."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"A page with many competing details may feel busy, but a crowded page is not automatically poor if the details serve a clear purpose. 包含许多互相竞争的细节的页面可能显得杂乱，但如果这些细节有明确的作用，内容丰富的页面也不一定不好。 Bāohán xǔduō hùxiāng jìngzhēng de xìjié de yèmiàn kěnéng xiǎnde záluàn, dàn rúguǒ zhèxiē xìjié yǒu míngquè de zuòyòng, nèiróng fēngfù de yèmiàn yě bù yídìng bù hǎo."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"Page turns 翻页设计 Fānyè shèjì"},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"The moment when a child turns a page can create surprise, suspense, or excitement. 儿童翻页的时刻可以带来惊喜、悬念或兴奋感。 Értóng fānyè de shíkè kěyǐ dàilái jīngxǐ, xuánniàn huò xīngfèn gǎn."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"An author may hide a character on the next page or delay revealing what happens. 作者可能把人物藏在下一页，或暂时不揭示接下来发生的事情。 Zuòzhě kěnéng bǎ rénwù cáng zài xià yí yè, huò zànshí bù jiēshì jiēxiàlái fāshēng de shìqing."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"Teachers can pause before turning the page and invite children to predict what may happen. 教师可以在翻页前暂停，并邀请儿童预测接下来可能发生的事情。 Jiàoshī kěyǐ zài fānyè qián zàntíng, bìng yāoqǐng értóng yùcè jiēxiàlái kěnéng fāshēng de shìqing."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"Double-page spreads 跨页设计 Kuàyè shèjì"},{"type":"image","figure":5,"src":"assets/topic2_figure_5.png","alt":"Topic 2 illustration, Figure 5"},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"Figure 5 — Double-page spread and gutter / 图五：跨页与中缝 / Tú wǔ: Kuàyè yǔ zhōngfèng"},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"Double-page spread — Two facing pages\n跨页——相对的两页\nKuàyè — Xiāngduì de liǎng yè"},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"Gutter — Centre fold\n中缝——中央折缝\nZhōngfèng — Zhōngyāng zhéfèng"},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"A double-page spread is an illustration or design that extends across two facing pages. 跨页设计是指延伸至相对两页的插图或版面安排。 Kuàyè shèjì shì zhǐ yánshēn zhì xiāngduì liǎng yè de chātú huò bǎnmiàn ānpái."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"It can show a large setting, an important event, or many details for children to explore. 它可以呈现广阔的场景、重要事件，或供儿童探索的许多细节。 Tā kěyǐ chéngxiàn guǎngkuò de chǎngjǐng, zhòngyào shìjiàn, huò gōng értóng tànsuǒ de xǔduō xìjié."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"Teachers should check whether the book's binding hides important information near the centre fold. 教师应该检查书籍的装订处是否遮住了靠近中间折缝的重要信息。 Jiàoshī yīnggāi jiǎnchá shūjí de zhuāngdìng chù shìfǒu zhēzhù le kàojìn zhōngjiān zhéfèng de zhòngyào xìnxī."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"Typography"},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"字体排版 Zìtǐ páibǎn"},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"Typography refers to the appearance, size, spacing, and arrangement of printed words. 字体排版是指文字的外观、大小、间距和排列方式。 Zìtǐ páibǎn shì zhǐ wénzì de wàiguān, dàxiǎo, jiānjù hé páiliè fāngshì."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"Clear typography helps children and adults read comfortably. 清晰的字体排版有助于儿童和成人舒适地阅读。 Qīngxī de zìtǐ páibǎn yǒuzhù yú értóng hé chéngrén shūshì de yuèdú."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"Font size and readability 字体大小与易读性 Zìtǐ dàxiǎo yǔ yìdúxìng"},{"type":"image","figure":6,"src":"assets/topic2_figure_6.png","alt":"Topic 2 illustration, Figure 6"},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"Figure 6 — Typography and readability / 图六：字体排版与易读性 / Tú liù: Zìtǐ páibǎn yǔ yìdúxìng"},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"Large font — Small font\n大字体——小字体\nDà zìtǐ — Xiǎo zìtǐ"},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"Clear spacing — Crowded spacing\n清晰的间距——拥挤的间距\nQīngxī de jiānjù — Yōngjǐ de jiānjù"},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"High contrast — Low contrast\n高对比度——低对比度\nGāo duìbǐdù — Dī duìbǐdù"},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"Text should be large enough for the intended readers and the reading situation. 文字大小应该适合目标读者及阅读情境。 Wénzì dàxiǎo yīnggāi shìhé mùbiāo dúzhě jí yuèdú qíngjìng."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"Very small text or crowded lines can make reading difficult. 过小的文字或过于拥挤的行距会增加阅读难度。 Guò xiǎo de wénzì huò guòyú yǒngjǐ de hángjù huì zēngjiā yuèdú nándù."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"Font style 字体样式 Zìtǐ yàngshì"},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"The font should suit the mood and purpose of the book while remaining easy to read. 字体应该符合书籍的气氛和目的，同时保持清晰易读。 Zìtǐ yīnggāi fúhé shūjí de qìfēn hé mùdì, tóngshí bǎochí qīngxī yìdú."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"Decorative fonts can be attractive, but using too many different styles may confuse readers. 装饰性字体可能很吸引人，但使用过多不同的字体样式可能让读者感到混乱。 Zhuāngshìxìng zìtǐ kěnéng hěn xīyǐn rén, dàn shǐyòng guòdù duō bùtóng de zìtǐ yàngshì kěnéng ràng dúzhě gǎndào hùnluàn."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"Spacing and contrast 间距与对比度 Jiānjù yǔ duìbǐdù"},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"Enough space between words and lines can help readers follow the text. 文字和行之间有足够的间距，可以帮助读者跟随内容阅读。 Wénzì hé háng zhījiān yǒu zúgòu de jiānjù, kěyǐ bāngzhù dúzhě gēnsuí nèiróng yuèdú."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"Strong contrast between text and background usually improves readability. 文字与背景之间有明显的对比度，通常可以提高易读性。 Wénzì yǔ bèijǐng zhījiān yǒu míngxiǎn de duìbǐdù, tōngcháng kěyǐ tígāo yìdúxìng."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"For example, dark text on a light background is often easier to read than pale text on a similar pale background. 例如，浅色背景上的深色文字，通常比浅色背景上的淡色文字更容易阅读。 Lìrú, qiǎnsè bèijǐng shàng de shēnsè wénzì, tōngcháng bǐ qiǎnsè bèijǐng shàng de dàn sè wénzì gèng róngyì yuèdú."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"Expressive typography 表现性字体排版 Biǎoxiànxìng zìtǐ páibǎn"},{"type":"image","figure":7,"src":"assets/topic2_figure_7.png","alt":"Topic 2 illustration, Figure 7"},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"Figure 7 — Expressive typography / 图七：表现性字体排版 / Tú qī: Biǎoxiànxìng zìtǐ páibǎn"},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"BOOM! — Loud voice\n砰！——大声\nPēng! — Dàshēng"},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"psst... — Quiet voice\n嘘……——轻声\nXū... — Qīngshēng"},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"Fast movement — Slow movement\n快速动作——缓慢动作\nKuàisù dòngzuò — Huǎnmàn dòngzuò"},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"The size or shape of words may change to show a character's voice, movement, or emotion. 文字的大小或形状可能会发生变化，以表现人物的声音、动作或情绪。 Wénzì de dàxiǎo huò xíngzhuàng kěnéng huì fāshēng biànhuà, yǐ biǎoxiàn rénwù de shēngyīn, dòngzuò huò qíngxù."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"For example, large letters may represent a loud shout, while small letters may suggest a whisper. 例如，大字可能表示大声呼喊，而小字可能表示轻声耳语。 Lìrú, dà zì kěnéng biǎoshì dàshēng hūhǎn, ér xiǎo zì kěnéng biǎoshì qīngshēng ěryǔ."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"This technique works best when it supports meaning and does not make the text difficult to read. 当这种技巧能够帮助表达意义而不会妨碍阅读时，效果最好。 Dāng zhè zhǒng jìqiǎo nénggòu bāngzhù biǎodá yìyì ér bú huì fáng'ài yuèdú shí, xiàoguǒ zuì hǎo."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"Integration of text and image"},{"type":"image","figure":8,"src":"assets/topic2_figure_8.png","alt":"Topic 2 illustration, Figure 8"},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"Figure 8 — Text and image relationships / 图八：文字与图像的关系 / Tú bā: Wénzì yǔ túxiàng de guānxì"},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"Pictures repeat the words\n图画重复文字的信息\nTúhuà chóngfù wénzì de xìnxī"},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"Pictures add information\n图画补充信息\nTúhuà bǔchōng xìnxī"},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"Pictures tell a different part\n图画呈现另一部分\nTúhuà chéngxiàn lìng yí bùfen"},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"文字与图像的结合 Wénzì yǔ túxiàng de jiéhé"},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"In a strong picture book, words and illustrations may share information, complement each other, or create different meanings. 在优秀的图画书中，文字与插图可以共同传递信息、互相补充，或产生不同的意义。 Zài yōuxiù de túhuàshū zhōng, wénzì yǔ chātú kěyǐ gòngtóng chuándì xìnxī, hùxiāng bǔchōng, huò chǎnshēng bùtóng de yìyì."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"1. The pictures repeat the words 1. 图画重复文字的信息 1. Túhuà chóngfù wénzì de xìnxī"},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"Sometimes the picture shows exactly what the words describe. 有时，图画呈现的内容与文字描述的内容完全相同。 Yǒushí, túhuà chéngxiàn de nèiróng yǔ wénzì miáoshù de nèiróng wánquán xiāngtóng."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"This can help younger children connect words with objects and actions. 这可以帮助年幼的儿童把词语与物品和动作联系起来。 Zhè kěyǐ bāngzhù niányòu de értóng bǎ cíyǔ yǔ wùpǐn hé dòngzuò liánxì qǐlái."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"2. The pictures add information 2. 图画补充信息 2. Túhuà bǔchōng xìnxī"},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"The words may tell only part of the story, while the pictures show extra details. 文字可能只讲述故事的一部分，而图画则呈现额外的细节。 Wénzì kěnéng zhǐ jiǎngshù gùshi de yí bùfen, ér túhuà zé chéngxiàn éwài de xìjié."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"For example, the words may say that a child is walking home, while the picture shows that the child is carrying a broken umbrella. 例如，文字可能只说一个孩子正在走路回家，而图画则显示孩子拿着一把破损的雨伞。 Lìrú, wénzì kěnéng zhǐ shuō yí ge háizi zhèngzài zǒulù huí jiā, ér túhuà zé xiǎnshì háizi názhe yì bǎ pòsǔn de yǔsǎn."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"Children can use these details to make inferences and ask questions. 儿童可以利用这些细节作出推断并提出问题。 Értóng kěyǐ lìyòng zhèxiē xìjié zuòchū tuīduàn bìng tíchū wèntí."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"3. The pictures tell a different part of the story 3. 图画呈现故事的另一部分 3. Túhuà chéngxiàn gùshi de lìng yí bùfen"},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"Sometimes, the words and pictures show different but related information. 有时，文字和图画会呈现不同但彼此相关的信息。 Yǒushí, wénzì hé túhuà huì chéngxiàn bùtóng dàn bǐcǐ xiāngguān de xìnxī."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"The words may say that a character is brave, while the picture shows the character hiding behind a chair. 文字可能说某个人物很勇敢，而图画却显示这个人物躲在椅子后面。 Wénzì kěnéng shuō mǒu ge rénwù hěn yǒnggǎn, ér túhuà què xiǎnshì zhège rénwù duǒ zài yǐzi hòumiàn."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"Children can discuss why the two sources of information seem different. 儿童可以讨论为什么这两种信息看起来有所不同。 Értóng kěyǐ tǎolùn wèishénme zhè liǎng zhǒng xìnxī kàn qǐlái yǒusuǒ bùtóng."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"4. The pictures create a surprise 4. 图画带来惊喜 4. Túhuà dàilái jīngxǐ"},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"An illustration may reveal something that the character or reader did not expect. 插图可能揭示人物或读者没有预料到的事情。 Chātú kěnéng jiēshì rénwù huò dúzhě méiyǒu yùliào dào de shìqing."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"This can encourage children to look closely, predict, and explain their thinking. 这可以鼓励儿童仔细观察、作出预测并解释自己的想法。 Zhè kěyǐ gǔlì értóng zǐxì guānchá, zuòchū yùcè bìng jiěshì zìjǐ de xiǎngfǎ."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"Practical activity: Read the pictures"},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"实践活动：阅读图画 Shíjiàn huódòng: Yuèdú túhuà"},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"Choose one page from a picture book and cover the words. 从一本图画书中选择一页，并遮住文字。 Cóng yì běn túhuàshū zhōng xuǎnzé yí yè, bìng zhēzhù wénzì."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"Ask what the children can learn from the illustration alone. 询问儿童仅通过插图能够发现什么。 Xúnwèn értóng jǐn tōngguò chātú nénggòu fāxiàn shénme."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"Then read the words and compare the information. 然后读出文字，并比较其中的信息。 Ránhòu dú chū wénzì, bìng bǐjiào qízhōng de xìnxī."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"Discuss whether the picture repeats, adds to, or changes the reader's understanding of the words. 讨论图画是重复、补充，还是改变了读者对文字的理解。 Tǎolùn túhuà shì chóngfù, bǔchōng, háishi gǎibiàn le dúzhě duì wénzì de lǐjiě."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"2.3 Developmental Appropriateness: Matching Books to the Child"},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"2.3 发展适宜性：为儿童选择合适的书籍 2.3 Fāzhǎn shìyíxìng: Wèi értóng xuǎnzé héshì de shūjí"},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"What is developmental appropriateness?"},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"什么是发展适宜性？ Shénme shì fāzhǎn shìyíxìng?"},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"Developmental appropriateness means choosing books that fit a child's current development, interests, experiences, and support needs. 发展适宜性是指选择符合儿童当前发展水平、兴趣、生活经验和支持需求的书籍。 Fāzhǎn shìyíxìng shì zhǐ xuǎnzé fúhé értóng dāngqián fāzhǎn shuǐpíng, xìngqù, shēnghuó jīngyàn hé zhīchí xūqiú de shūjí."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"Age is useful to consider, but age alone does not tell teachers everything about a child. 年龄是一个有用的参考因素，但仅凭年龄无法全面了解儿童。 Niánlíng shì yí ge yǒuyòng de cānkǎo yīnsù, dàn jǐn píng niánlíng wúfǎ quánmiàn liǎojiě értóng."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"Children of the same age may differ in language, attention, interests, background knowledge, and ways of communicating. 同龄儿童在语言、注意力、兴趣、背景知识和沟通方式方面可能有所不同。 Tónglíng értóng zài yǔyán, zhùyìlì, xìngqù, bèijǐng zhīshi hé gōutōng fāngshì fāngmiàn kěnéng yǒusuǒ bùtóng."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"A suitable book should offer some challenge without overwhelming the child. 合适的书籍应该提供一定的挑战，但不应让儿童感到难以应付。 Héshì de shūjí yīnggāi tígōng yídìng de tiǎozhàn, dàn bù yīng ràng értóng gǎndào nányǐ yìngfù."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"Considering the child's age and stage"},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"考虑儿童的年龄与发展阶段 Kǎolǜ értóng de niánlíng yǔ fāzhǎn jiēduàn"},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"The following are general suggestions rather than strict rules. 以下是一般性的建议，而不是严格的规定。 Yǐxià shì yìbān xìng de jiànyì, ér bú shì yángé de guīdìng."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"Babies and young toddlers 婴儿与年幼的幼儿 Yīng'ér yǔ niányòu de yòu'ér"},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"Babies and young toddlers often enjoy books with clear pictures, familiar objects, simple sounds, and repeated words. 婴儿和年幼的幼儿通常喜欢图画清晰、包含熟悉物品、简单声音和重复词语的书籍。 Yīng'ér hé niányòu de yòu'ér tōngcháng xǐhuan túhuà qīngxī, bāohán shúxī wùpǐn, jiǎndān shēngyīn hé chóngfù cíyǔ de shūjí."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"Short shared-reading sessions can fit their attention and daily routines. 简短的共读活动可以配合他们的注意力和日常作息。 Jiǎnduǎn de gòngdú huódòng kěyǐ pèihé tāmen de zhùyìlì hé rìcháng zuòxī."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"Board books may be useful because they are easier to handle and often more durable. 硬纸板书可能很实用，因为它们较容易拿取，而且通常更耐用。 Yìngzhǐbǎn shū kěnéng hěn shíyòng, yīnwèi tāmen jiào róngyì náqǔ, érqiě tōngcháng gèng nàiyòng."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"Adults can name objects, imitate sounds, sing, and respond to the child's gestures or vocalisations. 成人可以说出物品的名称、模仿声音、唱歌，并回应儿童的手势或发声。 Chéngrén kěyǐ shuō chū wùpǐn de míngchēng, mófǎng shēngyīn, chànggē, bìng huíyìng értóng de shǒushì huò fāshēng."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"Preschool children 学龄前儿童 Xué líng qián értóng"},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"Preschool children may enjoy stories with clear events, repeated phrases, humour, patterns, and characters they can understand. 学龄前儿童可能喜欢情节清晰、句子重复、富有幽默、具有规律，并且人物容易理解的故事。 Xué líng qián értóng kěnéng xǐhuan qíngjié qīngxī, jùzi chóngfù, fùyǒu yōumò, jùyǒu guīlǜ, bìngqiě rénwù róngyì lǐjiě de gùshi."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"They may enjoy predicting what happens next and explaining how a character feels. 他们可能喜欢预测接下来发生的事情，并解释人物的感受。 Tāmen kěnéng xǐhuan yùcè jiēxiàlái fāshēng de shìqing, bìng jiěshì rénwù de gǎnshòu."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"Books can include everyday experiences, imaginary adventures, family relationships, friendship, and simple information about the world. 书籍可以包含日常生活经验、想象中的冒险、家庭关系、友谊以及有关世界的简单知识。 Shūjí kěyǐ bāohán rìcháng shēnghuó jīngyàn, xiǎngxiàng zhōng de màoxiǎn, jiātíng guānxì, yǒuyì yǐjí yǒuguān shìjiè de jiǎndān zhīshi."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"Older preschool children 年龄较大的学龄前儿童 Niánlíng jiào dà de xué líng qián értóng"},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"Older preschool children may be ready for longer stories, more complex events, richer vocabulary, and different viewpoints. 年龄较大的学龄前儿童可能已经能够理解较长的故事、更复杂的事件、更丰富的词汇和不同的观点。 Niánlíng jiào dà de xué líng qián értóng kěnéng yǐjīng nénggòu lǐjiě jiào cháng de gùshi, gèng fùzá de shìjiàn, gèng fēngfù de cíhuì hé bùtóng de guāndiǎn."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"They may enjoy discussing why characters act in certain ways and how problems could be solved differently. 他们可能喜欢讨论人物为什么这样做，以及问题还可以怎样解决。 Tāmen kěnéng xǐhuan tǎolùn rénwù wèishénme zhèyàng zuò, yǐjí wèntí hái kěyǐ zěnyàng jiějué."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"Teachers should still observe each child rather than assume that all children are ready for the same book. 教师仍然应该观察每个儿童，而不是假设所有儿童都已经准备好阅读同一本书。 Jiàoshī réngrán yīnggāi guānchá měi ge értóng, ér bú shì jiǎshè suǒyǒu értóng dōu yǐjīng zhǔnbèi hǎo yuèdú tóng yì běn shū."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"Language and cultural background"},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"语言与文化背景 Yǔyán yǔ wénhuà bèijǐng"},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"A child's home language is an important part of learning and identity. 儿童的家庭语言是学习与身份认同的重要部分。 Értóng de jiātíng yǔyán shì xuéxí yǔ shēnfèn rèntóng de zhòngyào bùfen."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"Teachers can select books in children's familiar languages and gradually introduce new words or additional languages. 教师可以选择儿童熟悉语言的书籍，并逐步引入新词语或其他语言。 Jiàoshī kěyǐ xuǎnzé értóng shúxī yǔyán de shūjí, bìng zhúbù yǐnrù xīn cíyǔ huò qítā yǔyán."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"In a multilingual Malaysian classroom, teachers might connect a story with Bahasa Melayu, Mandarin, Tamil, English, or languages used in local communities. 在马来西亚的多语课堂中，教师可以把故事与马来语、华语、泰米尔语、英语或当地社区使用的语言联系起来。 Zài Mǎláixīyà de duōyǔ kètáng zhōng, jiàoshī kěyǐ bǎ gùshi yǔ Mǎláiyǔ, Huáyǔ, Tàimǐ'ěryǔ, Yīngyǔ huò dāngdì shèqū shǐyòng de yǔyán liánxì qǐlái."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"Teachers do not need to speak every home language to show respect for it. 教师不需要会说每一种家庭语言，也能表达对这些语言的尊重。 Jiàoshī bù xūyào huì shuō měi yì zhǒng jiātíng yǔyán, yě néng biǎodá duì zhèxiē yǔyán de zūnzhòng."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"They can invite families to share correct pronunciations, songs, stories, or meaningful words when families are comfortable doing so. 如果家庭愿意，教师可以邀请他们分享正确的发音、歌曲、故事或有意义的词语。 Rúguǒ jiātíng yuànyì, jiàoshī kěyǐ yāoqǐng tāmen fēnxiǎng zhèngquè de fāyīn, gēqǔ, gùshi huò yǒu yìyì de cíyǔ."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"Interests and life experiences"},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"兴趣与生活经验 Xìngqù yǔ shēnghuó jīngyàn"},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"Children are more likely to engage with books that connect with their interests and experiences. 儿童更容易投入与自己的兴趣和生活经验有关的书籍。 Értóng gèng róngyì tóurù yǔ zìjǐ de xìngqù hé shēnghuó jīngyàn yǒuguān de shūjí."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"Some children enjoy animals, vehicles, cooking, nature, music, or stories about family life. 有些儿童喜欢动物、交通工具、烹饪、大自然、音乐或家庭生活故事。 Yǒuxiē értóng xǐhuan dòngwù, jiāotōng gōngjù, pēngrèn, dà zìrán, yīnyuè huò jiātíng shēnghuó gùshi."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"A teacher can use these interests to introduce new ideas and vocabulary. 教师可以利用这些兴趣来引入新想法和词汇。 Jiàoshī kěyǐ lìyòng zhèxiē xìngqù lái yǐnrù xīn xiǎngfǎ hé cíhuì."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"Books can also introduce unfamiliar experiences in a respectful and understandable way. 书籍也可以用尊重且容易理解的方式介绍儿童不熟悉的经历。 Shūjí yě kěyǐ yòng zūnzhòng qiě róngyì lǐjiě de fāngshì jièshào értóng bù shúxī de jīnglì."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"For example, a story about visiting a clinic may help children understand what happens during a health check. 例如，关于去诊所的故事可以帮助儿童了解健康检查时会发生什么。 Lìrú, guānyú qù zhěnsuǒ de gùshi kěyǐ bāngzhù értóng liǎojiě jiànkāng jiǎnchá shí huì fāshēng shénme."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"Teachers should avoid assuming that every child has the same family structure, home resources, or life experiences. 教师应该避免假设每个儿童都有相同的家庭结构、家庭资源或生活经验。 Jiàoshī yīnggāi bìmiǎn jiǎshè měi ge értóng dōu yǒu xiāngtóng de jiātíng jiégòu, jiātíng zīyuán huò shēnghuó jīngyàn."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"Matching books to children with different abilities"},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"为不同能力的儿童选择合适的书籍 Wèi bùtóng nénglì de értóng xuǎnzé héshì de shūjí"},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"Children learn and communicate in different ways. 儿童以不同的方式学习和沟通。 Értóng yǐ bùtóng de fāngshì xuéxí hé gōutōng."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"A child may understand a story but find spoken responses difficult. 儿童可能理解故事，却觉得用口语回答有困难。 Értóng kěnéng lǐjiě gùshi, què juéde yòng kǒuyǔ huídá yǒu kùnnan."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"Another child may need larger print, tactile materials, clearer pictures, shorter reading sessions, or additional time. 另一个儿童可能需要较大的字体、触觉材料、更清晰的图画、较短的阅读时间或更多时间。 Lìng yí ge értóng kěnéng xūyào jiào dà de zìtǐ, chùjué cáiliào, gèng qīngxī de túhuà, jiào duǎn de yuèdú shíjiān huò gèng duō shíjiān."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"Teachers can support participation by using gestures, objects, picture symbols, communication boards, or assistive technology when appropriate. 教师可以在适当时使用手势、实物、图片符号、沟通板或辅助科技来支持儿童参与。 Jiàoshī kěyǐ zài shìdàng shí shǐyòng shǒushì, shíwù, túpiàn fúhào, gōutōng bǎn huò fǔzhù kējì lái zhīchí értóng cānyù."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"Children should not be excluded from rich stories simply because they use fewer spoken words or need additional support. 不应该仅仅因为儿童说的话较少或需要额外支持，就让他们无法接触丰富的故事。 Bù yīnggāi jǐnjǐn yīnwèi értóng shuō de huà jiào shǎo huò xūyào éwài zhīchí, jiù ràng tāmen wúfǎ jiēchù fēngfù de gùshi."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"The aim is to make the story accessible while preserving its meaning and enjoyment. 目标是在保留故事意义与乐趣的同时，让儿童能够接触和理解故事。 Mùbiāo shì zài bǎoliú gùshi yìyì yǔ lèqù de tóngshí, ràng értóng nénggòu jiēchù hé lǐjiě gùshi."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"Emotional readiness and sensitive topics"},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"情感准备与敏感主题 Qínggǎn zhǔnbèi yǔ mǐngǎn zhǔtí"},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"Some stories include separation, illness, grief, conflict, or frightening events. 有些故事涉及分离、疾病、悲伤、冲突或令人害怕的事件。 Yǒuxiē gùshi shèjí fēnlí, jíbìng, bēishāng, chōngtū huò lìng rén hàipà de shìjiàn."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"These topics can be valuable, but teachers should consider the children's needs and the context. 这些主题可能很有价值，但教师应该考虑儿童的需求与具体情境。 Zhèxiē zhǔtí kěnéng hěn yǒu jiàzhí, dàn jiàoshī yīnggāi kǎolǜ értóng de xūqiú yǔ jùtǐ qíngjìng."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"Before reading, teachers can check whether the book handles the topic carefully and provides opportunities for reassurance or discussion. 阅读前，教师可以检查书籍是否谨慎地处理主题，并提供安慰或讨论的机会。 Yuèdú qián, jiàoshī kěyǐ jiǎnchá shūjí shìfǒu jǐnshèn de chǔlǐ zhǔtí, bìng tígōng ānwèi huò tǎolùn de jīhuì."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"Children should not be forced to share personal experiences or feelings. 不应该强迫儿童分享个人经历或感受。 Bù yīnggāi qiǎngpò értóng fēnxiǎng gèrén jīnglì huò gǎnshòu."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"They may choose to speak, draw, act, listen quietly, or pass. 他们可以选择说话、画画、表演、安静聆听或暂时不参与。 Tāmen kěyǐ xuǎnzé shuōhuà, huàhuà, biǎoyǎn, ānjìng língtīng huò zànshí bù cānyù."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"Reading difficulty and appropriate challenge"},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"阅读难度与适当挑战 Yuèdú nándù yǔ shìdàng tiǎozhàn"},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"A book can be suitable even when it contains a few unfamiliar words or ideas. 即使书中包含一些陌生的词语或想法，它仍然可能适合儿童。 Jíshǐ shū zhōng bāohán yìxiē mòshēng de cíyǔ huò xiǎngfǎ, tā réngrán kěnéng shìhé értóng."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"Teachers can explain new words, connect them to familiar experiences, and use pictures or actions to support understanding. 教师可以解释新词语，将它们与熟悉的经验联系起来，并利用图画或动作帮助理解。 Jiàoshī kěyǐ jiěshì xīn cíyǔ, jiāng tāmen yǔ shúxī de jīngyàn liánxì qǐlái, bìng lìyòng túhuà huò dòngzuò bāngzhù lǐjiě."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"However, a book may be too difficult at that moment if children cannot follow the main events even with suitable support. 然而，如果即使提供适当支持，儿童仍然无法理解主要情节，那么这本书在当时可能太难了。 Rán'ér, rúguǒ jíshǐ tígōng shìdàng zhīchí, értóng réngrán wúfǎ lǐjiě zhǔyào qíngjié, nàme zhè běn shū zài dāngshí kěnéng tài nán le."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"Teachers can reread the book later, shorten the reading session, or choose another book before returning to it. 教师可以稍后再次阅读这本书、缩短阅读时间，或先选择另一本书，以后再回来阅读。 Jiàoshī kěyǐ shāohòu zàicì yuèdú zhè běn shū, suōduǎn yuèdú shíjiān, huò xiān xuǎnzé lìng yì běn shū, yǐhòu zài huílái yuèdú."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"The goal is not to choose only easy books, but to give children a supported path toward new learning. 目标不是只选择简单的书，而是为儿童提供有支持的学习途径，让他们逐步学习新内容。 Mùbiāo bú shì zhǐ xuǎnzé jiǎndān de shū, ér shì wèi értóng tígōng yǒu zhīchí de xuéxí tújìng, ràng tāmen zhúbù xuéxí xīn nèiróng."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"A simple book-selection checklist"},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"简单的选书检查清单 Jiǎndān de xuǎnshū jiǎnchá qīngdān"},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"Before choosing a book, teachers can ask the following questions. 选择书籍前，教师可以提出以下问题。 Xuǎnzé shūjí qián, jiàoshī kěyǐ tíchū yǐxià wèntí."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"- Is the story engaging and meaningful? 故事是否有趣并具有意义？ Gùshi shìfǒu yǒuqù bìng jùyǒu yìyì?"},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"- Do the words and illustrations work well together? 文字与插图是否配合得当？ Wénzì yǔ chātú shìfǒu pèihé dé dàng?"},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"- Is the text clear and comfortable to read? 文字是否清晰且容易阅读？ Wénzì shìfǒu qīngxī qiě róngyì yuèdú?"},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"- Does the book respect different cultures, families, and abilities? 这本书是否尊重不同的文化、家庭和能力？ Zhè běn shū shìfǒu zūnzhòng bùtóng de wénhuà, jiātíng hé nénglì?"},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"- Does the content suit the child's interests, experiences, and current development? 内容是否符合儿童的兴趣、经验和当前发展水平？ Nèiróng shìfǒu fúhé értóng de xìngqù, jīngyàn hé dāngqián fāzhǎn shuǐpíng?"},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"- Can children with different communication and support needs participate? 有不同沟通方式和支持需求的儿童能否参与？ Yǒu bùtóng gōutōng fāngshì hé zhīchí xūqiú de értóng néngfǒu cānyù?"},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"- Is the physical or digital format safe and practical to use? 实体或数码形式是否安全且方便使用？ Shítǐ huò shùmǎ xíngshì shìfǒu ānquán qiě fāngbiàn shǐyòng?"},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"- What could children learn, wonder about, or discuss after reading? 阅读后，儿童可以学习什么、对什么感到好奇，或讨论什么？ Yuèdú hòu, értóng kěyǐ xuéxí shénme, duì shénme gǎndào hàoqí, huò tǎolùn shénme?"},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"No book needs to be perfect in every area. 没有一本书需要在每个方面都达到完美。 Méiyǒu yì běn shū xūyào zài měi ge fāngmiàn dōu dádào wánměi."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"Teachers should consider the book's strengths, limitations, purpose, and suitability for the children who will use it. 教师应该考虑书籍的优点、局限、目的，以及它是否适合将要阅读的儿童。 Jiàoshī yīnggāi kǎolǜ shūjí de yōudiǎn, júxiàn, mùdì, yǐjí tā shìfǒu shìhé jiāngyào yuèdú de értóng."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"Practical activity: Choose the right book for the child"},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"实践活动：为儿童选择合适的书 Shíjiàn huódòng: Wèi értóng xuǎnzé héshì de shū"},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"Imagine that you are selecting a book for a four-year-old child who enjoys animals and is beginning to use longer sentences. 假设你正在为一名四岁、喜欢动物并开始使用较长句子的儿童选择书籍。 Jiǎshè nǐ zhèngzài wèi yì míng sì suì, xǐhuan dòngwù bìng kāishǐ shǐyòng jiào cháng jùzi de értóng xuǎnzé shūjí."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"Compare two books, one with clear pictures and a simple repeating story, and another with long paragraphs and few illustrations. 比较两本书，一本有清晰的图画和简单的重复故事，另一本则有较长的段落和较少的插图。 Bǐjiào liǎng běn shū, yì běn yǒu qīngxī de túhuà hé jiǎndān de chóngfù gùshi, lìng yì běn zé yǒu jiào cháng de duànluò hé jiào shǎo de chātú."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"Decide which book you would try first and explain why. 决定你会先尝试哪一本书，并解释原因。 Juédìng nǐ huì xiān chángshì nǎ yì běn shū, bìng jiěshì yuányīn."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"Then consider how your choice might change if the child uses picture symbols to communicate or has a strong interest in factual animal information. 接着思考，如果儿童使用图片符号沟通，或特别喜欢动物知识，你的选择可能会有什么变化。 Jiēzhe sīkǎo, rúguǒ értóng shǐyòng túpiàn fúhào gōutōng, huò tèbié xǐhuan dòngwù zhīshi, nǐ de xuǎnzé kěnéng huì yǒu shénme biànhuà."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"There may be more than one suitable choice when teachers can explain their reasons and provide the right support. 如果教师能够解释选择的理由并提供适当支持，那么可能不止一本书是合适的。 Rúguǒ jiàoshī nénggòu jiěshì xuǎnzé de lǐyóu bìng tígōng shìdàng zhīchí, nàme kěnéng bù zhǐ yì běn shū shì héshì de."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"Topic Summary"},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"主题总结 Zhǔtí zǒngjié"},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"High-quality children's literature combines meaningful content, effective storytelling, and thoughtful artistic choices. 优质儿童文学结合有意义的内容、有效的叙事和用心的艺术设计。 Yōuzhì értóng wénxué jiéhé yǒu yìyì de nèiróng, yǒuxiào de xùshì hé yòngxīn de yìshù shèjì."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"A good picture book uses words and illustrations to support, enrich, or sometimes challenge each other's meaning. 优秀的图画书运用文字与插图互相支持、丰富，有时也会对彼此表达的意义提出挑战。 Yōuxiù de túhuàshū yùnyòng wénzì yǔ chātú hùxiāng zhīchí, fēngfù, yǒushí yě huì duì bǐcǐ biǎodá de yìyì tíchū tiǎozhàn."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"Format, layout, typography, and page turns influence how children experience a book. 书籍形式、版面设计、字体排版和翻页方式都会影响儿童的阅读体验。 Shūjí xíngshì, bǎnmiàn shèjì, zìtǐ páibǎn hé fānyè fāngshì dōu huì yǐngxiǎng értóng de yuèdú tǐyàn."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"Book selection should consider development, language, interests, cultural experiences, emotional readiness, and accessibility. 选书时应该考虑儿童的发展、语言、兴趣、文化经验、情感准备和无障碍需求。 Xuǎnshū shí yīnggāi kǎolǜ értóng de fāzhǎn, yǔyán, xìngqù, wénhuà jīngyàn, qínggǎn zhǔnbèi hé wú zhàng'ài xūqiú."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"A book does not have to be perfect, but teachers should understand its strengths and limitations. 一本书不必在所有方面都完美，但教师应该了解它的优点与局限。 Yì běn shū bù bì zài suǒyǒu fāngmiàn dōu wánměi, dàn jiàoshī yīnggāi liǎojiě tā de yōudiǎn yǔ júxiàn."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"The most suitable book is one that meets a clear purpose and gives the particular children opportunities to enjoy, understand, and engage. 最合适的书籍是能够满足明确目的，并让特定儿童有机会享受、理解和参与的书籍。 Zuì héshì de shūjí shì nénggòu mǎnzú míngquè mùdì, bìng ràng tèdìng értóng yǒu jīhuì xiǎngshòu, lǐjiě hé cānyù de shūjí."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"Key Terms"},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"关键词 Guānjiàn cíyǔ"},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"Literary quality refers to the strength of the story, language, characters, and ideas. 文学品质是指故事、语言、人物和想法的质量。 Wénxué pǐnzhì shì zhǐ gùshi, yǔyán, rénwù hé xiǎngfǎ de zhìliàng."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"Artistic merit refers to the effectiveness and quality of illustrations and visual design. 艺术价值是指插图和视觉设计的品质与表现效果。 Yìshù jiàzhí shì zhǐ chātú hé shìjué shèjì de pǐnzhì yǔ biǎoxiàn xiàoguǒ."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"Format refers to the physical or digital form of a book. 书籍形式是指书籍的实体或数码形态。 Shūjí xíngshì shì zhǐ shūjí de shítǐ huò shùmǎ xíngtài."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"Layout refers to how words, pictures, and spaces are arranged. 版面设计是指文字、图画和空间的排列方式。 Bǎnmiàn shèjì shì zhǐ wénzì, túhuà hé kōngjiān de páiliè fāngshì."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"Typography refers to the style, size, spacing, and arrangement of text. 字体排版是指文字的样式、大小、间距和排列方式。 Zìtǐ páibǎn shì zhǐ wénzì de yàngshì, dàxiǎo, jiānjù hé páiliè fāngshì."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"Double-page spread refers to a design that extends across two facing pages. 跨页设计是指延伸至相对两页的设计。 Kuàyè shèjì shì zhǐ yánshēn zhì xiāngduì liǎng yè de shèjì."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"Developmental appropriateness means matching books to a child's development and individual needs. 发展适宜性是指选择符合儿童发展水平和个别需求的书籍。 Fāzhǎn shìyíxìng shì zhǐ xuǎnzé fúhé értóng fāzhǎn shuǐpíng hé gèbié xūqiú de shūjí."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"Stereotype means an overly simple or unfair idea about a group of people. 刻板印象是指对某个群体过度简单或不公平的看法。 Kèbǎn yìnxiàng shì zhǐ duì mǒu ge qúntǐ guòdù jiǎndān huò bù gōngpíng de kànfǎ."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"Accessibility means making books and reading experiences usable by children with different needs. 无障碍性是指让有不同需求的儿童都能够使用书籍并参与阅读体验。 Wú zhàng'ài xìng shì zhǐ ràng yǒu bùtóng xūqiú de értóng dōu nénggòu shǐyòng shūjí bìng cānyù yuèdú tǐyàn."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"Reflection Questions"},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"反思问题 Fǎnsī wèntí"},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"1. What makes a picture book high quality beyond having attractive illustrations? 除了插图吸引人之外，什么特点能使一本图画书成为优质作品？ Chúle chātú xīyǐn rén zhīwài, shénme tèdiǎn néng shǐ yì běn túhuàshū chéngwéi yōuzhì zuòpǐn?"},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"2. How can pictures provide information that the words do not tell us? 图画如何提供文字没有告诉我们的信息？ Túhuà rúhé tígōng wénzì méiyǒu gàosu wǒmen de xìnxī?"},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"3. How might font size, layout, and page turns affect a child's reading experience? 字体大小、版面设计和翻页方式可能如何影响儿童的阅读体验？ Zìtǐ dàxiǎo, bǎnmiàn shèjì hé fānyè fāngshì kěnéng rúhé yǐngxiǎng értóng de yuèdú tǐyàn?"},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"4. How can teachers choose books that respect children's languages, cultures, families, and abilities? 教师如何选择尊重儿童语言、文化、家庭和能力的书籍？ Jiàoshī rúhé xuǎnzé zūnzhòng értóng yǔyán, wénhuà, jiātíng hé nénglì de shūjí?"},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"5. What would you change to make a book more accessible for a child who communicates without speech? 如果要让一本书更适合不使用口语沟通的儿童，你会作出什么调整？ Rúguǒ yào ràng yì běn shū gèng shìhé bù shǐyòng kǒuyǔ gōutōng de értóng, nǐ huì zuòchū shénme tiáozhěng?"},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"6. Why should teachers consider more than age when selecting a book? 为什么教师选书时应该考虑年龄以外的因素？ Wèishénme jiàoshī xuǎnshū shí yīnggāi kǎolǜ niánlíng yǐwài de yīnsù?"},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"Final Takeaway"},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"最后的重点 Zuìhòu de zhòngdiǎn"},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"Choosing a book is a teaching decision, not just a shopping decision. 选择书籍是一项教学决定，而不只是购买书籍的决定。 Xuǎnzé shūjí shì yí xiàng jiàoxué juédìng, ér bú zhǐ shì gòumǎi shūjí de juédìng."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"Teachers should look beyond the cover and ask what the book offers, whom it includes, and how children may experience it. 教师应该超越封面，思考这本书能带来什么、包含哪些人，以及儿童可能如何体验它。 Jiàoshī yīnggāi chāoyuè fēngmiàn, sīkǎo zhè běn shū néng dàilái shénme, bāohán nǎxiē rén, yǐjí értóng kěnéng rúhé tǐyàn tā."},{"type":"paragraph","style":"Normal","text":"A thoughtful choice can turn story time into an opportunity for language, imagination, connection, and belonging. 用心的选书能够把故事时间变成促进语言、想象、联系与归属感的机会。 Yòngxīn de xuǎnshū nénggòu bǎ gùshi shíjiān biànchéng cùjìn yǔyán, xiǎngxiàng, liánxì yǔ guīshǔgǎn de jīhuì."}];
const topic2Questions=[{"title":["Question 1 — Literary quality","第一题——文学品质","Dì yī tí — Wénxué pǐnzhì"],"stem":["A teacher is choosing a picture book for a preschool class. Which feature is the strongest sign of good literary quality?","一位教师正在为幼儿班选择一本图画书。哪一项最能体现作品具有良好的文学品质？","Yí wèi jiàoshī zhèngzài wèi yòu'é bān xuǎnzé yì běn túhuà shū. Nǎ yí xiàng zuì néng tǐxiàn zuòpǐn jùyǒu liánghǎo de wénxué pǐnzhì?"],"options":[["A. Choose the book with the most detailed information because children learn more when a story includes many facts.","选择信息最详细的图书，因为故事包含大量事实时，幼儿能够学到更多知识。","Xuǎnzé xìnxī zuì xiángxì de túshū, yīnwèi gùshì bāohán dàliàng shìshí shí, yòu'ér nénggòu xuédào gèng duō zhīshi."],["B. Choose the book with the most exciting events because a fast-moving plot is the clearest sign of literary quality.","选择情节最刺激的图书，因为节奏快速的情节最能体现文学品质。","Xuǎnzé qíngjié zuì cìjī de túshū, yīnwèi jiézòu kuàisù de qíngjié zuì néng tǐxiàn wénxué pǐnzhì."],["C. Choose the book with the richest vocabulary because sophisticated language makes a story more literary.","选择词汇最丰富的图书，因为较复杂的语言能使故事更具文学性。","Xuǎnzé cíhuì zuì fēngfù de túshū, yīnwèi jiào fùzá de yǔyán néng shǐ gùshì gèng jù wénxuéxìng."],["D. Evaluate how the characters, language, plot, and ending work together to create a meaningful and engaging story.","评估人物、语言、情节和结局如何相互配合，共同构成有意义且引人入胜的故事。","Pínggū rénwù, yǔyán, qíngjié hé jiéjú rúhé xiānghù pèihé, gòngtóng gòuchéng yǒu yìyì qiě yǐnrénrùshèng de gùshì."]],"correct":3,"explanations":["- A: Facts can enrich a story, but factual detail alone does not establish literary quality. 事实可以丰富故事，但仅有大量事实并不能证明故事具有良好的文学品质。 Shìshí kěyǐ fēngfù gùshì, dàn jǐn yǒu dàliàng shìshí bìng bù néng zhèngmíng gùshì jùyǒu liánghǎo de wénxué pǐnzhì.","- B: An exciting plot can engage readers, but excitement alone does not guarantee a meaningful, well-developed story. 刺激的情节可以吸引读者，但刺激感本身不能保证故事有意义且发展完整。 Cìjī de qíngjié kěyǐ xīyǐn dúzhě, dàn cìjīgǎn běnshēn bù néng bǎozhèng gùshì yǒu yìyì qiě fāzhǎn wánzhěng.","- C: Rich vocabulary may strengthen a story, but difficult language may also be unsuitable for its intended readers. 丰富的词汇可能增强故事的表现力，但艰深的语言也可能不适合目标读者。 Fēngfù de cíhuì kěnéng zēngqiáng gùshì de biǎoxiànlì, dàn jiānshēn de yǔyán yě kěnéng bù shìhé mùbiāo dúzhě.","- D: This evaluates several connected literary features rather than relying on one feature alone. 这个选项综合评估多个相互关联的文学要素，而不是只依赖单一要素。 Zhège xuǎnxiàng zōnghé pínggū duō ge xiānghù guānlián de wénxué yàosù, ér bùshì zhǐ yīlài dānyī yàosù."]},{"title":["Question 2 — Artistic merit","第二题——艺术价值","Dì èr tí — Yìshù jiàzhí"],"stem":["A picture book has a simple story, but its illustrations use colour, shape, and page composition to show a character's growing fear. What does this best demonstrate?","一本图画书的故事很简单，但插图运用颜色、形状和页面构图来表现角色逐渐增加的恐惧。这最能说明什么？","Yì běn túhuà shū de gùshi hěn jiǎndān, dàn chātú yùnyòng yánsè, xíngzhuàng hé yèmiàn gòutú lái biǎoxiàn juésè zhújiàn zēngjiā de kǒngjù. Zhè zuì néng shuōmíng shénme?"],"options":[["A. Artistic merit depends mainly on how realistic the pictures look.","艺术价值主要取决于图画看起来有多写实。","Yìshù jiàzhí zhǔyào qǔjué yú túhuà kàn qǐlái yǒu duō xiěshí."],["B. Illustrations are successful only when they show exactly what the words describe.","只有当插图完全呈现文字所描述的内容时，插图才算成功。","Zhǐyǒu dāng chātú wánquán chéngxiàn wénzì suǒ miáoshù de nèiróng shí, chātú cái suàn chénggōng."],["C. Artistic choices can communicate feelings and add meaning to a story.","艺术表现手法能够传达情感，并为故事增添意义。","Yìshù biǎoxiàn shǒufǎ nénggòu chuándá qínggǎn, bìng wèi gùshi zēngtiān yìyì."],["D. Illustrations should use as many colours and details as possible.","插图应该尽可能使用更多颜色和细节。","Chātú yīnggāi jǐn kěnéng shǐyòng gèng duō yánsè hé xìjié."]],"correct":2,"explanations":["A. Realistic art can be effective, but stylised, abstract, or imaginative illustrations can also have strong artistic merit.","B. Illustrations can repeat the words, but they can also add information or communicate feelings that the words do not state.","C. Colour, shape, and composition can guide readers' attention and help them understand a character's emotions.","D. More detail does not always improve a picture; artistic choices should serve the story and its intended readers."]},{"title":["Question 3 — Representation and inclusion","第三题——人物呈现与包容性","Dì sān tí — Rénwù chéngxiàn yǔ bāoróngxìng"],"stem":["A teacher is selecting a story for a Malaysian preschool with children from different cultural backgrounds. Which choice is most appropriate?","一位教师正在为一所拥有不同文化背景幼儿的马来西亚幼儿园选择故事。哪一种选择最合适？","Yí wèi jiàoshī zhèngzài wèi yì suǒ yōngyǒu bùtóng wénhuà bèijǐng yòu'ér de Mǎláixīyà yòu'éryuán xuǎnzé gùshi. Nǎ yì zhǒng xuǎnzé zuì héshì?"],"options":[["A. Select books that include characters from different backgrounds, even when those characters have little influence on the story.","选择包含不同背景人物的图书，即使这些人物对故事的发展影响不大。","Xuǎnzé bāohán bùtóng bèijǐng rénwù de túshū, jíshǐ zhèxiē rénwù duì gùshì de fāzhǎn yǐngxiǎng bù dà."],["B. Prefer books that present familiar cultural practices because these are easier for young children to understand.","优先选择呈现熟悉文化习俗的图书，因为幼儿比较容易理解这些内容。","Yōuxiān xuǎnzé chéngxiàn shúxī wénhuà xísú de túshū, yīnwèi yòu'ér bǐjiào róngyì lǐjiě zhèxiē nèiróng."],["C. Examine whether characters from different backgrounds are represented respectfully, with meaningful roles and individual personalities.","检查不同背景的人物是否得到尊重性的呈现，并拥有有意义的角色和鲜明的个性。","Jiǎnchá bùtóng bèijǐng de rénwù shìfǒu dédào zūnzhòngxìng de chéngxiàn, bìng yōngyǒu yǒu yìyì de juésè hé xiānmíng de gèxìng."],["D. Prefer books that avoid mentioning cultural differences so that all children can focus on similarities.","优先选择不提及文化差异的图书，让所有幼儿都能把注意力放在相似之处。","Yōuxiān xuǎnzé bù tíjí wénhuà chāyì de túshū, ràng suǒyǒu yòu'ér dōu néng bǎ zhùyìlì fàng zài xiāngsì zhī chù."]],"correct":2,"explanations":["- A: A diverse cast is a useful starting point, but simply including a character does not ensure meaningful representation. 多元化的人物阵容是一个良好的起点，但仅仅加入某类人物并不能确保有意义的呈现。 Duōyuánhuà de rénwù zhènróng shì yí ge liánghǎo de qǐdiǎn, dàn jǐnjǐn jiārù mǒu lèi rénwù bìng bù néng quèbǎo yǒu yìyì de chéngxiàn.","- B: Familiar practices may help children connect with a story, but books should not be limited to familiar cultures. 熟悉的习俗可以帮助幼儿与故事建立联系，但图书不应只呈现熟悉的文化。 Shúxī de xísú kěyǐ bāngzhù yòu'ér yǔ gùshì jiànlì liánxì, dàn túshū bù yīng zhǐ chéngxiàn shúxī de wénhuà.","- C: This considers both who appears in the book and how each character is portrayed. 这个选项同时考虑书中出现了哪些人物，以及每个人物是如何被描绘的。 Zhège xuǎnxiàng tóngshí kǎolǜ shū zhōng chūxiàn le nǎxiē rénwù, yǐjí měi ge rénwù shì rúhé bèi miáohuì de.","- D: Shared experiences can connect readers, but avoiding differences may make some children’s identities invisible. 共同的经历可以连接读者，但刻意避开差异可能使某些幼儿的身份与经历被忽视。 Gòngtóng de jīnglì kěyǐ liánjiē dúzhě, dàn kèyì bìkāi chāyì kěnéng shǐ mǒuxiē yòu'ér de shēnfèn yǔ jīnglì bèi hūshì."]},{"title":["Question 4 — Choosing a format for babies","第四题——为婴儿选择图书形式","Dì sì tí — Wèi yīng'ér xuǎnzé túshū xíngshì"],"stem":["A teacher wants babies to explore a book by touching, turning pages, and looking at pictures. Which book format is generally the most suitable starting point?","一位教师希望婴儿通过触摸、翻页和观看图画来探索书籍。哪一种书籍形式通常最适合作为起点？","Yí wèi jiàoshī xīwàng yīng'ér tōngguò chùmō, fānyè hé guānkàn túhuà lái tànsuǒ shūjí. Nǎ yì zhǒng shūjí xíngshì tōngcháng zuì shìhé zuòwéi qǐdiǎn?"],"options":[["A. Choose a large picture book with detailed illustrations because an adult can hold it while the baby looks.","选择一本图画丰富的大开本图书，因为成人可以拿着书让婴儿观看。","Xuǎnzé yì běn túhuà fēngfù de dà kāiběn túshū, yīnwèi chéngrén kěyǐ názhe shū ràng yīng'ér guānkàn."],["B. Choose a sturdy board book with manageable pages, clear images, and opportunities for the baby to handle it safely.","选择一本结实的硬页书，页面容易翻动、图像清晰，并方便婴儿安全地拿取和探索。","Xuǎnzé yì běn jiēshi de yìngyèshū, yèmiàn róngyì fāndòng, túxiàng qīngxī, bìng fāngbiàn yīng'ér ānquán de náqǔ hé tànsuǒ."],["C. Choose a cloth book in every case because babies are not yet ready to benefit from paper books.","无论什么情况都选择布书，因为婴儿还不能从纸质图书中受益。","Wúlùn shénme qíngkuàng dōu xuǎnzé bùshū, yīnwèi yīng'ér hái bù néng cóng zhǐzhì túshū zhōng shòuyì."],["D. Choose a book with short sentences and realistic pictures because babies benefit most from direct verbal explanations.","选择句子简短、图画写实的图书，因为婴儿最能从直接的语言解释中受益。","Xuǎnzé jùzi jiǎnduǎn, túhuà xiěshí de túshū, yīnwèi yīng'ér zuì néng cóng zhíjiē de yǔyán jiěshì zhōng shòuyì."]],"correct":1,"explanations":["- A: Large images can be engaging during shared reading, but the format may be less manageable for a baby to explore independently. 大幅图像可以吸引婴儿共同阅读，但这种形式可能不太方便婴儿独立探索。 Dà fú túxiàng kěyǐ xīyǐn yīng'ér gòngtóng yuèdú, dàn zhè zhǒng xíngshì kěnéng bù tài fāngbiàn yīng'ér dúlì tànsuǒ.","- B: A sturdy, manageable format supports safe handling, sensory exploration, and shared reading. 结实且容易操作的形式有助于安全翻阅、感官探索和共同阅读。 Jiēshi qiě róngyì cāozuò de xíngshì yǒuzhù yú ānquán fānyuè, gǎnguān tànsuǒ hé gòngtóng yuèdú.","- C: Cloth books can be suitable, but they are not the only useful format for babies. 布书可能很适合婴儿，但并不是唯一有用的图书形式。 Bùshū kěnéng hěn shìhé yīng'ér, dàn bìng bú shì wéiyī yǒuyòng de túshū xíngshì.","- D: Short language and realistic pictures may help in some situations, but format, safety, and opportunities to explore also matter. 简短的语言和写实图画在某些情况下可能有帮助，但图书形式、安全性和探索机会同样重要。 Jiǎnduǎn de yǔyán hé xiěshí túhuà zài mǒuxiē qíngkuàng xià kěnéng yǒu bāngzhù, dàn túshū xíngshì, ānquánxìng hé tànsuǒ jīhuì tóngyàng zhòngyào."]},{"title":["Question 5 — Layout, page turns, and suspense","第五题——版面设计、翻页与悬念","Dì wǔ tí — Bǎnmiàn shèjì, fānyè yǔ xuánniàn"],"stem":["During a read-aloud, the teacher notices that the final illustration on one page hides what will happen next. Turning the page reveals a surprising event. What design feature is being used effectively?","在朗读活动中，教师发现某一页最后的插图没有显示接下来会发生什么。翻到下一页后，一个令人惊讶的事件出现了。这里有效运用了哪一种设计特点？","Zài lǎngdú huódòng zhōng, jiàoshī fāxiàn mǒu yí yè zuìhòu de chātú méiyǒu xiǎnshì jiēxiàlái huì fāshēng shénme. Fān dào xià yí yè hòu, yí gè lìng rén jīngyà de shìjiàn chūxiàn le. Zhèlǐ yǒuxiào yùnyòng le nǎ yì zhǒng shèjì tèdiǎn?"],"options":[["A. Use the same layout on every spread so children can predict where to look and are not distracted by changes.","每个跨页都使用相同的版面，让幼儿能够预测阅读位置，避免因变化而分心。","Měi ge kuàyè dōu shǐyòng xiāngtóng de bǎnmiàn, ràng yòu'ér nénggòu yùcè yuèdú wèizhì, bìmiǎn yīn biànhuà ér fēnxīn."],["B. Place the main character and all important information on the left page so children can understand the scene before turning the page.","把主角和所有重要信息放在左页，让幼儿翻页前就能理解整个场景。","Bǎ zhǔjué hé suǒyǒu zhòngyào xìnxī fàng zài zuǒ yè, ràng yòu'ér fānyè qián jiù néng lǐjiě zhěnggè chǎngjǐng."],["C. Keep each page visually balanced by avoiding empty space and placing a similar amount of information on every spread.","通过避免留白，并在每个跨页放置相近数量的信息，使每一页看起来都很平衡。","Tōngguò bìmiǎn liúbái, bìng zài měi ge kuānyè fàngzhì xiāngjìn shùliàng de xìnxī, shǐ měi yí yè kàn qǐlái dōu hěn pínghéng."],["D. Examine how spacing, image placement, and page turns guide attention and reveal information at an effective moment.","分析留白、图像位置和翻页如何引导注意力，并在适当的时刻揭示信息。","Fēnxī liúbái, túxiàng wèizhì hé fānyè rúhé yǐndǎo zhùyìlì, bìng zài shìdàng de shíkè jiēshì xìnxī."]],"correct":3,"explanations":["- A: Predictable layouts can support orientation, but using the same layout everywhere may reduce opportunities to create emphasis or suspense. 可预测的版面有助于幼儿定位，但处处使用相同版面可能减少强调重点或营造悬念的机会。 Kě yùcè de bǎnmiàn yǒuzhù yú yòu'ér dìngwèi, dàn chùchù shǐyòng xiāngtóng bǎnmiàn kěnéng jiǎnshǎo qiángdiào zhòngdiǎn huò yíngzào xuánniàn de jīhuì.","- B: Showing important information early can help comprehension, but revealing everything before a page turn may weaken a planned surprise. 提前呈现重要信息可以帮助理解，但在翻页前揭示所有内容可能削弱预设的惊喜。 Tíqián chéngxiàn zhòngyào xìnxī kěyǐ bāngzhù lǐjiě, dàn zài fānyè qián jiēshì suǒyǒu nèiróng kěnéng xuēruò yùshè de jīngxǐ.","- C: Visual balance can be useful, but empty space and uneven information can be deliberate artistic choices. 视觉平衡可能很有帮助，但留白和信息分布不均也可能是刻意的艺术选择。 Shìjué pínghéng kěnéng hěn yǒu bāngzhù, dàn liúbái hé xìnxī fēnbù bù jūn yě kěnéng shì kèyì de yìshù xuǎnzé.","- D: This considers layout as a storytelling tool, not simply a way to arrange content neatly. 这个选项把版面设计视为讲故事的工具，而不只是整齐排列内容的方法。 Zhège xuǎnxiàng bǎ bǎnmiàn shèjì shìwéi jiǎng gùshì de gōngjù, ér bù zhǐ shì zhěngqí páiliè nèiróng de fāngfǎ."]},{"title":["Question 6 — Typography and readability","第六题——字体设计与可读性","Dì liù tí — Zìtǐ shèjì yǔ kě dúxìng"],"stem":["A teacher finds a picture book with beautiful illustrations, but the text is printed in a very small, decorative font against a busy background. What is the most important concern?","一位教师找到一本插图精美的图画书，但文字使用非常小的装饰字体，并印在复杂的背景上。最重要的考虑是什么？","Yí wèi jiàoshī zhǎodào yì běn chātú jīngměi de túhuà shū, dàn wénzì shǐyòng fēicháng xiǎo de zhuāngshì zìtǐ, bìng yìn zài fùzá de bèijǐng shàng. Zuì zhòngyào de kǎolǜ shì shénme?"],"options":[["A. Select type that is clear at the intended viewing size, with suitable spacing and a style that fits the book without reducing readability.","选择在预定阅读尺寸下清晰易读、间距适当，并且风格符合图书特点而不影响阅读的字体。","Xuǎnzé zài yùdìng yuèdú chǐcùn xià qīngxī yì dú, jiānjù shìdàng, bìngqiě fēnggé fúhé túshū tèdiǎn ér bù yǐngxiǎng yuèdú de zìtǐ."],["B. Choose decorative lettering that reflects the story’s mood because visual expression is more important than consistent readability.","选择能够表现故事氛围的装饰性字体，因为视觉表现比持续保持易读性更重要。","Xuǎnzé nénggòu biǎoxiàn gùshì fēnwéi de zhuāngshìxìng zìtǐ, yīnwèi shìjué biǎoxiàn bǐ chíxù bǎochí yì dúxìng gèng zhòngyào."],["C. Use the largest available type throughout because larger letters always make a picture book easier for every child to read.","全书都使用尽可能大的字体，因为较大的字母总能让每个孩子更容易阅读图画书。","Quán shū dōu shǐyòng jǐn kěnéng dà de zìtǐ, yīnwèi jiào dà de zìmǔ zǒng néng ràng měi ge háizi gèng róngyì yuèdú túhuàshū."],["D. Keep the same type size and style on every page because consistency matters more than the relationship between text and illustration.","每页都使用相同的字号和字体风格，因为一致性比文字与插画之间的关系更重要。","Měi yè dōu shǐyòng xiāngtóng de zìhào hé zìtǐ fēnggé, yīnwèi yízhìxìng bǐ wénzì yǔ chāhuà zhījiān de guānxì gèng zhòngyào."]],"correct":0,"explanations":["- A: Readability depends on more than size; spacing, contrast, type style, and intended readers also matter. 可读性不仅取决于字号，还取决于间距、对比度、字体风格和目标读者。 Kě dúxìng bùjǐn qǔjué yú zìhào, hái qǔjué yú jiānjù, duìbǐdù, zìtǐ fēnggé hé mùbiāo dúzhě.","- B: Decorative lettering can contribute to mood, but it should not make the words unnecessarily difficult to read. 装饰性字体可以营造氛围，但不应使文字变得不必要地难以阅读。 Zhuāngshìxìng zìtǐ kěyǐ yíngzào fēnwéi, dàn bù yīng shǐ wénzì biàn de bù bìyào de nányǐ yuèdú.","- C: Larger type may help some readers, but excessively large type can disrupt layout and does not automatically suit every child. 较大的字体可能帮助某些读者，但过大的字体可能破坏版面，也不一定适合每个孩子。 Jiào dà de zìtǐ kěnéng bāngzhù mǒuxiē dúzhě, dàn guò dà de zìtǐ kěnéng pòhuài bǎnmiàn, yě bù yídìng shìhé měi ge háizi.","- D: Consistency can help readers, but typography may need to change when emphasis, pacing, or the text-image relationship calls for it. 一致性可以帮助读者，但当重点、节奏或文字与图像的关系有所需要时，字体设计也可能需要变化。 Yízhìxìng kěyǐ bāngzhù dúzhě, dàn dāng zhòngdiǎn, jiézòu huò wénzì yǔ túxiàng de guānxì yǒu suǒ xūyào shí, zìtǐ shèjì yě kěnéng xūyào biànhuà."]},{"title":["Question 7 — The relationship between text and image","第七题——文字与图像的关系","Dì qī tí — Wénzì yǔ túxiàng de guānxì"],"stem":["The words in a picture book say, “Mei was not afraid.” However, the illustration shows Mei hiding behind her mother and looking worried. What should the teacher recognise?","一本图画书的文字写着：“美一点也不害怕。”然而，插图却显示美一躲在妈妈身后，神情担忧。教师应该认识到什么？","Yì běn túhuà shū de wénzì xiězhe: “Měi Yì yìdiǎn yě bù hàipà.” Rán'ér, chātú què xiǎnshì Měi Yì duǒ zài māma shēnhòu, shénqíng dānyōu. Jiàoshī yīnggāi rènshi dào shénme?"],"options":[["A. Treat the written sentence as the most reliable source and use the illustration mainly to confirm its literal meaning.","把文字句子视为最可靠的信息来源，并主要利用插画确认文字的字面意思。","Bǎ wénzì jùzi shìwéi zuì kěkào de xìnxī láiyuán, bìng zhǔyào lìyòng chāhuà quèrèn wénzì de zìmiàn yìsi."],["B. Assume the illustration corrects the sentence and teaches the reader what the character is actually feeling.","假设插画是在纠正句子，并告诉读者人物实际上有什么感受。","Jiǎshè chāhuà shì zài jiūzhèng jùzi, bìng gàosu dúzhě rénwù shíjì shàng yǒu shénme gǎnshòu."],["C. Consider whether the contrast between the character’s words and visible expression reveals an emotion or meaning that neither communicates alone.","思考人物说的话与可见表情之间的对比，是否揭示了两者单独呈现时无法表达的情绪或意义。","Sīkǎo rénwù shuō de huà yǔ kějiàn biǎoqíng zhījiān de duìbǐ, shìfǒu jiēshì le liǎng zhě dāndú chéngxiàn shí wúfǎ biǎodá de qíngxù huò yìyì."],["D. Treat the difference as an illustration error unless the written story directly explains why the character looks different from what they say.","除非文字故事直接解释人物为什么言行不一，否则把这种差异视为插画错误。","Chúfēi wénzì gùshì zhíjiē jiěshì rénwù wèishénme yánxíng bù yī, fǒuzé bǎ zhè zhǒng chāyì shìwéi chāhuà cuòwù."]],"correct":2,"explanations":["- A: Words provide important information, but illustrations may add meaning rather than merely repeat the text. 文字提供重要信息，但插画可能增加新的意义，而不只是重复文字。 Wénzì tígōng zhòngyào xìnxī, dàn chāhuà kěnéng zēngjiā xīn de yìyì, ér bù zhǐ shì chóngfù wénzì.","- B: The illustration may reveal a hidden feeling, but it should be interpreted with attention to the whole story rather than treated as an automatic correction. 插画可能揭示隐藏的情绪，但应结合整个故事进行解读，而不是自动视为对文字的纠正。 Chāhuà kěnéng jiēshì yǐncáng de qíngxù, dàn yīng jiéhé zhěnggè gùshì jìnxíng jiědú, ér bùshì zìdòng shìwéi duì wénzì de jiūzhèng.","- C: The contrast may create irony, reveal unspoken feelings, or invite readers to make an inference. 这种对比可能产生反讽、揭示未说出的感受，或引导读者进行推理。 Zhè zhǒng duìbǐ kěnéng chǎnshēng fǎnfěng, jiēshì wèi shuō chū de gǎnshòu, huò yǐndǎo dúzhě jìnxíng tuīlǐ.","- D: A difference between text and image can be intentional and meaningful, rather than an error. 文字与图像之间的差异可能是有意且有意义的，而不是错误。 Wénzì yǔ túxiàng zhījiān de chāyì kěnéng shì yǒuyì qiě yǒu yìyì de, ér bùshì cuòwù."]},{"title":["Question 8 — Matching a book to a four-year-old","第八题——为四岁幼儿选择合适的图书","Dì bā tí — Wèi sì suì yòu'ér xuǎnzé héshì de túshū"],"stem":["A four-year-old enjoys talking about animals but is still learning to follow long spoken sentences. Which book is likely to be the best starting point?","一名四岁幼儿喜欢谈论动物，但仍在学习理解较长的口语句子。哪一种书最适合作为起点？","Yì míng sì suì yòu'ér xǐhuan tánlùn dòngwù, dàn réng zài xuéxí lǐjiě jiào cháng de kǒuyǔ jùzi. Nǎ yì zhǒng shū zuì shìhé zuòwéi qǐdiǎn?"],"options":[["A. Choose a book with very short sentences and familiar words, even if the story offers little opportunity to explore the child’s interest in animals.","选择句子很短、词语熟悉的图书，即使故事很少让幼儿探索自己对动物的兴趣。","Xuǎnzé jùzi hěn duǎn, cíyǔ shúxī de túshū, jíshǐ gùshì hěn shǎo ràng yòu'ér tànsuǒ zìjǐ duì dòngwù de xìngqù."],["B. Choose an engaging animal story with supportive illustrations and manageable language, while allowing opportunities to discuss new words.","选择一本有趣的动物故事，配有辅助理解的插画和适量的语言，并提供讨论新词语的机会。","Xuǎnzé yì běn yǒuqù de dòngwù gùshì, pèi yǒu fǔzhù lǐjiě de chāhuà hé shìliàng de yǔyán, bìng tígōng tǎolùn xīn cíyǔ de jīhuì."],["C. Choose a detailed nonfiction animal book because factual information is more educational than a narrative for a four-year-old.","选择一本内容详细的动物知识书，因为对四岁幼儿而言，事实信息比故事叙述更有教育价值。","Xuǎnzé yì běn nèiróng xiángxì de dòngwù zhīshi shū, yīnwèi duì sì suì yòu'ér ér yán, shìshí xìnxī bǐ gùshì xùshù gèng yǒu jiàoyù jiàzhí."],["D. Choose a story with challenging language to extend vocabulary, relying on the adult to explain unfamiliar sentences as they appear.","选择语言有挑战性的故事来扩展词汇，并依靠成人在遇到陌生句子时逐一解释。","Xuǎnzé yǔyán yǒu tiǎozhànxìng de gùshì lái kuòzhǎn cíhuì, bìng yīkào chéngrén zài yùdào mòshēng jùzi shí zhúyī jiěshì."]],"correct":1,"explanations":["- A: Accessible language is helpful, but the book should also connect with the child’s interests and provide worthwhile engagement. 容易理解的语言很有帮助，但图书也应联系幼儿的兴趣，并提供有价值的阅读体验。 Róngyì lǐjiě de yǔyán hěn yǒu bāngzhù, dàn túshū yě yīng liánxì yòu'ér de xìngqù, bìng tígōng yǒu jiàzhí de yuèdú tǐyàn.","- B: This balances the child’s interest, language needs, visual support, and opportunities to learn. 这个选项兼顾幼儿的兴趣、语言需要、视觉支持和学习机会。 Zhège xuǎnxiàng jiāngù yòu'ér de xìngqù, yǔyán xūyào, shìjué zhīchí hé xuéxí jīhuì.","- C: Nonfiction can be valuable, but the best choice depends on the child and the purpose, not on the assumption that facts are always superior to stories. 非虚构读物很有价值，但最佳选择取决于幼儿和阅读目的，而不是假设事实总比故事更好。 Fēi xūgòu dúwù hěn yǒu jiàzhí, dàn zuìjiā xuǎnzé qǔjué yú yòu'ér hé yuèdú mùdì, ér bùshì jiǎshè shìshí zǒng bǐ gùshì gèng hǎo.","- D: New language can extend learning, but excessive difficulty may make the story harder to follow and reduce independent participation. 新语言可以拓展学习，但难度过高可能使故事难以理解，并减少幼儿自主参与的机会。 Xīn yǔyán kěyǐ tuòzhǎn xuéxí, dàn nándù guò gāo kěnéng shǐ gùshì nányǐ lǐjiě, bìng jiǎnshǎo yòu'ér zìzhǔ cānyù de jīhuì."]},{"title":["Question 9 — Inclusive participation","第九题——包容性参与","Dì jiǔ tí — Bāoróngxìng cānyù"],"stem":["A preschool teacher wants to include a child who communicates mainly through pointing and picture symbols during story time. Which approach best supports participation?","一位幼儿园教师希望一名主要通过指物和图片符号进行沟通的幼儿参与故事时间。哪一种做法最能支持这名幼儿参与？","Yí wèi yòu'éryuán jiàoshī xīwàng yì míng zhǔyào tōngguò zhǐwù hé túpiàn fúhào jìnxíng gōutōng de yòu'ér cānyù gùshi shíjiān. Nǎ yì zhǒng zuòfǎ zuì néng zhīchí zhè míng yòu'ér cānyù?"],"options":[["A. Ask the child to practise spoken answers first so that they can gradually participate in the same way as their peers.","先让幼儿练习口头回答，使他们逐渐能够像同伴一样参与活动。","Xiān ràng yòu'ér liànxí kǒutóu huídá, shǐ tāmen zhújiàn nénggòu xiàng tóngbàn yíyàng cānyù huódòng."],["B. Let the child observe the activity until they are ready to use words, then invite them to answer aloud.","让幼儿先观察活动，直到他们准备好使用语言，再邀请他们大声回答。","Ràng yòu'ér xiān guānchá huódòng, zhídào tāmen zhǔnbèi hǎo shǐyòng yǔyán, zài yāoqǐng tāmen dàshēng huídá."],["C. Give the child the same picture choices as peers but ask an adult to interpret the child’s selection for the group.","给幼儿与同伴相同的图片选项，但请成人向小组解释幼儿的选择。","Gěi yòu'ér yǔ tóngbàn xiāngtóng de túpiàn xuǎnxiàng, dàn qǐng chéngrén xiàng xiǎozǔ jiěshì yòu'ér de xuǎnzé."],["D. Accept pointing or picture symbols as meaningful responses, offer accessible choices, and allow the child time to respond.","接受指认或图片符号作为有意义的回应，提供容易使用的选项，并给予幼儿足够的回应时间。","Jiēshòu zhǐrèn huò túpiàn fúhào zuòwéi yǒu yìyì de huíyìng, tígōng róngyì shǐyòng de xuǎnxiàng, bìng jǐyǔ yòu'ér zúgòu de huíyìng shíjiān."]],"correct":3,"explanations":["- A: Speech practice may be useful when appropriate, but spoken language should not be a condition for participating in the activity. 在适当情况下，口语练习可能有帮助，但口头表达不应成为参与活动的条件。 Zài shìdàng qíngkuàng xià, kǒuyǔ liànxí kěnéng yǒu bāngzhù, dàn kǒutóu biǎodá bù yīng chéngwéi cānyù huódòng de tiáojiàn.","- B: Waiting may reduce pressure, but it can also delay participation unnecessarily if accessible communication is already available. 等待可能减轻压力，但如果已有可使用的沟通方式，也可能不必要地延迟幼儿参与。 Děngdài kěnéng jiǎnqīng yālì, dàn rúguǒ yǐ yǒu kě shǐyòng de gōutōng fāngshì, yě kěnéng bù bìyào de yánchí yòu'ér cānyù.","- C: Picture choices can support communication, but relying on an adult to interpret every response may reduce the child’s direct agency. 图片选项可以支持沟通，但每次都依赖成人解释回应，可能削弱幼儿直接表达和自主参与的机会。 Túpiàn xuǎnxiàng kěyǐ zhīchí gōutōng, dàn měi cì dōu yīlài chéngrén jiěshì huíyìng, kěnéng xuēruò yòu'ér zhíjiē biǎodá hé zìzhǔ cānyù de jīhuì.","- D: This recognises the child’s existing communication methods and supports meaningful participation without requiring speech. 这个选项认可幼儿现有的沟通方式，并在不要求口语表达的情况下支持有意义的参与。 Zhège xuǎnxiàng rènkě yòu'ér xiànyǒu de gōutōng fāngshì, bìng zài bù yāoqiú kǒuyǔ biǎodá de qíngkuàng xià zhīchí yǒu yìyì de cānyù."]},{"title":["Question 10 — Making a balanced book-selection decision","第十题——作出全面的图书选择决定","Dì shí tí — Zuòchū quánmiàn de túshū xuǎnzé juédìng"],"stem":["A teacher is choosing between two books for a preschool class. Book A has beautiful illustrations but presents a cultural group through a hurtful stereotype. Book B has simpler illustrations, a coherent story, and respectful characters from different backgrounds. Which is the better decision?","一位教师正在为幼儿班选择两本书中的一本。A书的插图很精美，但通过伤人的刻板印象描绘某个文化群体。B书的插图较简单，故事连贯，角色也尊重不同的文化背景。哪一个选择更好？","Yí wèi jiàoshī zhèngzài wèi yòu'ér bān xuǎnzé liǎng běn shū zhōng de yì běn. A shū de chātú hěn jīngměi, dàn tōngguò shāngrén de kèbǎn yìnxiàng miáohuì mǒu gè wénhuà qúntǐ. B shū de chātú jiào jiǎndān, gùshi liánguàn, juésè yě zūnzhòng bùtóng de wénhuà bèijǐng. Nǎ yí gè xuǎnzé gèng hǎo?"],"options":[["A. Prefer the book with respectful characters and a coherent, engaging story, while recognising that simpler illustrations can still serve the story well.","优先选择人物呈现尊重、故事连贯且引人入胜的图书，同时认识到较简单的插画也能很好地服务故事。","Yōuxiān xuǎnzé rénwù chéngxiàn zūnzhòng, gùshì liánguàn qiě yǐnrénrùshèng de túshū, tóngshí rènshi dào jiào jiǎndān de chāhuà yě néng hěn hǎo de fúwù gùshì."],["B. Prefer the book with the strongest visual technique because artistic sophistication can make children question and discuss stereotypes.","优先选择视觉技巧最出色的图书，因为高超的艺术表现可以促使幼儿思考和讨论刻板印象。","Yōuxiān xuǎnzé shìjué jìqiǎo zuì chūsè de túshū, yīnwèi gāochāo de yìshù biǎoxiàn kěyǐ cùshǐ yòu'ér sīkǎo hé tǎolùn kèbǎn yìnxiàng."],["C. Use the book with the simpler illustrations for younger children and reserve the book with more complex artwork for older children.","为年龄较小的幼儿选择插画较简单的图书，把艺术表现较复杂的图书留给年龄较大的儿童。","Wèi niánlíng jiào xiǎo de yòu'ér xuǎnzé chāhuà jiào jiǎndān de túshū, bǎ yìshù biǎoxiàn jiào fùzá de túshū liú gěi niánlíng jiào dà de értóng."],["D. Choose either book according to the children’s immediate preferences because engagement is more important than the specific strengths and weaknesses of a book.","根据幼儿当下的喜好选择任意一本，因为参与兴趣比图书的具体优缺点更重要。","Gēnjù yòu'ér dāngxià de xǐhào xuǎnzé rènyì yì běn, yīnwèi cānyù xìngqù bǐ túshū de jùtǐ yōu quē diǎn gèng zhòngyào."]],"correct":0,"explanations":["- A: This weighs respectful representation, narrative quality, and artistic suitability together instead of expecting every strength in one book to be equally strong. 这个选项综合考虑尊重性的人物呈现、叙事品质和艺术适切性，而不是要求一本书的每个方面都同样出色。 Zhège xuǎnxiàng zōnghé kǎolǜ zūnzhòngxìng de rénwù chéngxiàn, xùshì pǐnzhì hé yìshù shìqièxìng, ér bùshì yāoqiú yì běn shū de měi ge fāngmiàn dōu tóngyàng chūsè.","- B: Strong artwork may prompt discussion, but artistic sophistication does not automatically make harmful stereotypes acceptable or educationally suitable. 出色的艺术表现可能引发讨论，但艺术技巧高超并不意味着有害的刻板印象就变得可以接受或适合教学。 Chūsè de yìshù biǎoxiàn kěnéng yǐnfā tǎolùn, dàn yìshù jìqiǎo gāochāo bìng bù yìwèizhe yǒuhài de kèbǎn yìnxiàng jiù biàn de kěyǐ jiēshòu huò shìhé jiàoxué.","- C: Illustration complexity alone is not a reliable way to decide age suitability; meaning, content, and the particular children also matter. 插画的复杂程度本身并不是判断年龄适切性的可靠依据；意义、内容和具体幼儿的需要同样重要。 Chāhuà de fùzá chéngdù běnshēn bìng bú shì pànduàn niánlíng shìqièxìng de kěkào yījù; yìyì, nèiróng hé jùtǐ yòu'ér de xūyào tóngyàng zhòngyào.","- D: Children’s preferences matter, but educators also need to evaluate quality, representation, and suitability rather than relying on immediate appeal alone. 幼儿的喜好很重要，但教育者也需要评估品质、人物呈现和适切性，而不能只依赖即时吸引力。 Yòu'ér de xǐhào hěn zhòngyào, dàn jiàoyùzhě yě xūyào pínggū pǐnzhì, rénwù chéngxiàn hé shìqièxìng, ér bù néng zhǐ yīlài jíshí xīyǐnlì."]}];
const topic2LecturerNotes=["Lecturer-facing quality check and teaching notes","These notes are for the lecturer, not part of the student quiz display. They can later be kept in the lecturer-only section of the app.","Question 1 — Literary quality","Teaching point: Literary quality involves the strength of the story, characters, language and storytelling—not just attractive pictures or a direct moral.","教学重点：文学品质包括故事、角色、语言和叙事表现，而不只是漂亮的图画或直接的道德教训。","Jiàoxué zhòngdiǎn: Wénxué pǐnzhì bāokuò gùshi, juésè, yǔyán hé xùshì biǎoxiàn, ér bù zhǐ shì piàoliang de túhuà huò zhíjiē de dàodé jiàoxùn.","Common misconception: A book is automatically good because it is colourful, educational or teaches a lesson.","常见误解：一本书只要色彩鲜艳、具有教育意义或传授道理，就一定是好书。","Chángjiàn wùjiě: Yì běn shū zhǐyào sècǎi xiānyàn, jùyǒu jiàoyù yìyì huò chuánshòu dàoli, jiù yídìng shì hǎo shū.","Discussion prompt: Can a book teach children something valuable without directly telling them what to do?","讨论问题：一本书能否在不直接告诉幼儿应该怎么做的情况下，教会他们有价值的东西？","Tǎolùn wèntí: Yì běn shū néngfǒu zài bù zhíjiē gàosu yòu'ér yīnggāi zěnme zuò de qíngkuàng xià, jiāohuì tāmen yǒu jiàzhí de dōngxi?","Question 2 — Artistic merit","Teaching point: Colour, shape, line, texture and composition can communicate mood and meaning. Realistic art is not the only form of quality illustration.","教学重点：颜色、形状、线条、质感和构图能够传达情绪与意义。写实艺术并不是优质插图的唯一形式。","Jiàoxué zhòngdiǎn: Yánsè, xíngzhuàng, xiàntiáo, zhìgǎn hé gòutú nénggòu chuándá qíngxù yǔ yìyì. Xiěshí yìshù bìng bú shì yōuzhì chātú de wéiyī xíngshì.","Common misconception: More colours, more details or more realistic pictures always mean better art.","常见误解：颜色越多、细节越多或图画越写实，艺术品质就一定越高。","Chángjiàn wùjiě: Yánsè yuè duō, xìjié yuè duō huò túhuà yuè xiěshí, yìshù pǐnzhì jiù yídìng yuè gāo.","Discussion prompt: How might dark colours, empty space or small figures help communicate fear or loneliness?","讨论问题：深色、留白或较小的人物形象，可以怎样帮助表达恐惧或孤独？","Tǎolùn wèntí: Shēnsè, liúbái huò jiào xiǎo de rénwù xíngxiàng, kěyǐ zěnyàng bāngzhù biǎodá kǒngjù huò gūdú?","Question 3 — Representation and inclusion","Teaching point: Look beyond whether a book includes different cultures. Consider how characters are portrayed and whether they have meaningful roles.","教学重点：不能只看一本书是否包含不同文化，还要考虑角色如何被描绘，以及他们是否具有实际意义。","Jiàoxué zhòngdiǎn: Bù néng zhǐ kàn yì běn shū shìfǒu bāohán bùtóng wénhuà, hái yào kǎolǜ juésè rúhé bèi miáohuì, yǐjí tāmen shìfǒu jùyǒu shíjì yìyì.","Common misconception: Including one character from a cultural group automatically makes a book inclusive.","常见误解：只要加入一个来自某个文化群体的角色，这本书就自动具有包容性。","Chángjiàn wùjiě: Zhǐyào jiārù yí gè láizì mǒu gè wénhuà qúntǐ de juésè, zhè běn shū jiù zìdòng jùyǒu bāoróng xìng.","Discussion prompt: What would respectful representation look like in a story about Malaysia's diverse communities?","讨论问题：在描写马来西亚多元社群的故事中，尊重不同群体的呈现应该是什么样的？","Tǎolùn wèntí: Zài miáohuì Mǎláixīyà duōyuán shèqún de gùshi zhōng, zūnzhòng bùtóng qúntǐ de chéngxiàn yīnggāi shì shénme yàng de?","Question 4 — Book format","Teaching point: The physical design of a book should suit children's motor abilities, interests and stage of development. Board books are often useful for babies, with adult supervision.","教学重点：书籍的实体设计应配合幼儿的动作能力、兴趣和发展阶段。硬纸板书通常适合婴儿探索，但仍需成人看护。","Jiàoxué zhòngdiǎn: Shūjí de shítǐ shèjì yīng pèihé yòu'ér de dòngzuò nénglì, xìngqù hé fāzhǎn jiēduàn. Yìng zhǐbǎn shū tōngcháng shìhé yīng'ér tànsuǒ, dàn réng xū chéngrén kānhù.","Common misconception: Any book labelled for children is automatically suitable for every child in that age group.","常见误解：只要标注为儿童读物，就一定适合该年龄组的每一个孩子。","Chángjiàn wùjiě: Zhǐyào biāozhù wéi értóng dúwù, jiù yídìng shìhé gāi niánlíng zǔ de měi yí gè háizi.","Discussion prompt: What features would you look for when choosing a book for a toddler who likes to handle books independently?","讨论问题：如果要为喜欢自己拿取书籍的幼儿选择书，你会注意哪些特点？","Tǎolùn wèntí: Rúguǒ yào wèi xǐhuan zìjǐ náqǔ shūjí de yòu'ér xuǎnzé shū, nǐ huì zhùyì nǎxiē tèdiǎn?","Question 5 — Layout and page turns","Teaching point: Page turns, double-page spreads, white space and visual placement can influence pacing, attention and suspense.","教学重点：翻页、跨页设计、留白和视觉元素的位置都会影响故事节奏、注意力和悬念。","Jiàoxué zhòngdiǎn: Fānyè, kuàyè shèjì, liúbái hé shìjué yuánsù de wèizhì dōu huì yǐngxiǎng gùshi jiézòu, zhùyì lì hé xuánniàn.","Common misconception: Layout is merely decoration and does not affect how a story is experienced.","常见误解：版面设计只是装饰，不会影响读者体验故事的方式。","Chángjiàn wùjiě: Bǎnmiàn shèjì zhǐ shì zhuāngshì, bú huì yǐngxiǎng dúzhě tǐyàn gùshi de fāngshì.","Discussion prompt: Where could an illustrator place a character to make readers curious about what happens next?","讨论问题：插画家可以把角色放在哪里，以引起读者对后续情节的好奇？","Tǎolùn wèntí: Chāhuàjiā kěyǐ bǎ juésè fàng zài nǎlǐ, yǐ yǐnqǐ dúzhě duì hòuxù qíngjié de hàoqí?","Question 6 — Typography","Teaching point: Font size, readability, spacing and contrast affect access to text. Decorative typography can be effective when used carefully.","教学重点：字号、可读性、间距和对比度都会影响读者阅读文字的能力。谨慎使用的装饰字体也可以发挥良好效果。","Jiàoxué zhòngdiǎn: Zìhào, kědúxìng, jiānjù hé duìbǐdù dōu huì yǐngxiǎng dúzhě yuèdú wénzì de nénglì. Jǐnshèn shǐyòng de zhuāngshì zìtǐ yě kěyǐ fāhuī liánghǎo xiàoguǒ.","Common misconception: A visually unusual font is automatically unsuitable, or children should simply work harder to read it.","常见误解：外观特别的字体一定不合适，或者幼儿只需要更努力地阅读就可以。","Chángjiàn wùjiě: Wàiguān tèbié de zìtǐ yídìng bù héshì, huòzhě yòu'ér zhǐ xūyào gèng nǔlì de yuèdú jiù kěyǐ.","Discussion prompt: How could a teacher adapt the reading experience if a child's vision or visual attention makes the printed text difficult to access?","讨论问题：如果幼儿的视觉能力或视觉注意力使他们难以阅读印刷文字，教师可以怎样调整阅读体验？","Tǎolùn wèntí: Rúguǒ yòu'ér de shìjué nénglì huò shìjué zhùyì lì shǐ tāmen nányǐ yuèdú yìnshuā wénzì, jiàoshī kěyǐ zěnyàng tiáozhěng yuèdú tǐyàn?","Question 7 — Text and image","Teaching point: Pictures may repeat, extend, complement or contradict the words. Readers should interpret both modes together.","教学重点：图画可以重复、扩展、补充或与文字形成矛盾。读者应该结合文字和图画进行理解。","Jiàoxué zhòngdiǎn: Túhuà kěyǐ chóngfù, kuòzhǎn, bǔchōng huò yǔ wénzì xíngchéng máodùn. Dúzhě yīnggāi jiéhé wénzì hé túhuà jìnxíng lǐjiě.","Common misconception: Illustrations must always show exactly what the text says.","常见误解：插图必须始终准确呈现文字所说的内容。","Chángjiàn wùjiě: Chātú bìxū shǐzhōng zhǔnquè chéngxiàn wénzì suǒ shuō de nèiróng.","Discussion prompt: What questions could a teacher ask children when the character's words and facial expression do not match?","讨论问题：当角色说的话与面部表情不一致时，教师可以向幼儿提出什么问题？","Tǎolùn wèntí: Dāng juésè shuō de huà yǔ miànbù biǎoqíng bù yízhì shí, jiàoshī kěyǐ xiàng yòu'ér tíchū shénme wèntí?","Question 8 — Developmental appropriateness","Teaching point: Choose books by considering age, language ability, interests, prior experiences and the level of challenge—not age alone.","教学重点：选择书籍时，应考虑年龄、语言能力、兴趣、已有经验和挑战程度，而不只是年龄。","Jiàoxué zhòngdiǎn: Xuǎnzé shūjí shí, yīng kǎolǜ niánlíng, yǔyán nénglì, xìngqù, yǐyǒu jīngyàn hé tiǎozhàn chéngdù, ér bù zhǐ shì niánlíng.","Common misconception: A book is suitable simply because its recommended age matches the child's age.","常见误解：只要书籍建议的年龄与幼儿的年龄相符，这本书就一定合适。","Chángjiàn wùjiě: Zhǐyào shūjí jiànyì de niánlíng yǔ yòu'ér de niánlíng xiāngfú, zhè běn shū jiù yídìng héshì.","Discussion prompt: How could the same book be adapted for children with different language abilities?","讨论问题：教师可以怎样调整同一本书的阅读方式，以适应不同语言能力的幼儿？","Tǎolùn wèntí: Jiàoshī kěyǐ zěnyàng tiáozhěng tóng yì běn shū de yuèdú fāngshì, yǐ shìyìng bùtóng yǔyán nénglì de yòu'ér?","Question 9 — Inclusive participation","Teaching point: Inclusion means enabling children to participate meaningfully through appropriate communication methods, accessible materials and sufficient response time.","教学重点：融合教育意味着通过适当的沟通方式、无障碍材料和充足的回应时间，让幼儿有意义地参与活动。","Jiàoxué zhòngdiǎn: Rónghé jiàoyù yìwèizhe tōngguò shìdàng de gōutōng fāngshì, wú zhàng'ài cáiliào hé chōngzú de huíyìng shíjiān, ràng yòu'ér yǒu yìyì de cānyù huódòng.","Common misconception: Children must speak in the same way or complete the same response to participate successfully.","常见误解：幼儿必须使用相同的说话方式或完成相同的回应，才算成功参与。","Chángjiàn wùjiě: Yòu'ér bìxū shǐyòng xiāngtóng de shuōhuà fāngshì huò wánchéng xiāngtóng de huíyìng, cái suàn chénggōng cānyù.","Discussion prompt: What alternative ways could children use to predict what happens next in a story?","讨论问题：幼儿还可以通过哪些替代方式，预测故事接下来会发生什么？","Tǎolùn wèntí: Yòu'ér hái kěyǐ tōngguò nǎxiē tìdài fāngshì, yùcè gùshi jiēxiàlái huì fāshēng shénme?","Question 10 — Balanced evaluation","Teaching point: High-quality selection involves the whole book: literary strength, artistic choices, representation, accessibility and suitability for the intended readers.","教学重点：选择优质图画书时，需要整体评估作品，包括文学表现、艺术设计、角色呈现、可及性，以及对目标读者的适切性。","Jiàoxué zhòngdiǎn: Xuǎnzé yōuzhì túhuà shū shí, xūyào zhěngtǐ pínggū zuòpǐn, bāokuò wénxué biǎoxiàn, yìshù shèjì, juésè chéngxiàn, kějí xìng, yǐjí duì mùbiāo dúzhě de shìqiè xìng.","Common misconception: One excellent feature, such as beautiful artwork, can compensate for every other weakness.","常见误解：只要有一个突出的优点，例如精美的插图，就能弥补其他所有缺点。","Chángjiàn wùjiě: Zhǐyào yǒu yí gè tūchū de yōudiǎn, lìrú jīngměi de chātú, jiù néng míbǔ qítā suǒyǒu quēdiǎn.","Discussion prompt: If a book has excellent illustrations but contains harmful stereotypes, what should a teacher consider before using it?","讨论问题：如果一本书的插图非常出色，却包含有害的刻板印象，教师在使用之前应该考虑什么？","Tǎolùn wèntí: Rúguǒ yì běn shū de chātú fēicháng chūsè, què bāohán yǒuhài de kèbǎn yìnxiàng, jiàoshī zài shǐyòng zhīqián yīnggāi kǎolǜ shénme?","Answer key and quality review","Quality review note: The current answer positions are somewhat concentrated in B and C. Before treating this as the final approved quiz, I recommend redistributing some correct answers across A–D while keeping the questions, distractor quality and explanations intact. This will reduce the chance that students can guess answers from a pattern.","质量审查说明：目前的正确答案较集中在B和C。正式批准这套测验之前，建议在保留题目、干扰选项质量和解释内容的前提下，重新分配部分正确答案至A至D，以减少学生根据答案规律猜题的机会。","Zhìliàng shěnchá shuōmíng: Mùqián de zhèngquè dá'àn jiào jízhōng zài B hé C. Zhèngshì pīzhǔn zhè tào cèyàn zhīqián, jiànyì zài bǎoliú tímù, gānrǎo xuǎnxiàng zhìliàng hé jiěshì nèiróng de qiántí xià, chóngxīn fēnpèi bùfèn zhèngquè dá'àn zhì A dào D, yǐ jiǎnshǎo xuéshēng gēnjù dá'àn guīlǜ cāi tí de jīhuì."];
const topic2Escape=(s)=>String(s).replace(/[&<>"']/g,c=>({'&':'&amp;','<':'&lt;','>':'&gt;','"':'&quot;',"'":'&#39;'}[c]));
const topic2Lines=(lines)=>lines.map(s=>'<span class="topic2Tri">'+topic2Escape(s)+'</span>').join('');
function openTopic2(){
 showView('lesson');
 const el=document.getElementById('lessonContent');
 let body='';
 const headingIndices=new Set([0,1,2,3,9,10,15,16,17,18,24,25,27,32,37,42,47,48,52,60,68,76,80,81,86,87,95,96,101,102,108,109,110,111,114,121,124,131,136,137,140,144,148,156,157,160,168,171,175,184,190,192,195,203,206,207,212,213,214,215,220,221,223,228,232,236,237,243,244,251,252,259,260,266,267,273,274,286,287,293,294,301,302,312,313,320,321]);
 const captionIndices=new Set([54,55,56,62,63,64,70,71,72,116,117,118,150,151,152,162,163,164,177,178,179,180]);
 for(const [idx,block] of topic2Lecture.entries()){
  if(block.type==='image'){
   const src=block.path||block.src||'';
   const img=src.split('/').pop();
   body+='<figure><img loading="lazy" src="./'+encodeURIComponent(img)+'" alt="Topic 2 illustration: '+topic2Escape(img)+'"></figure>';
  }else if(block.type==='paragraph'){
   const txt=block.text||'';
   const isHead=headingIndices.has(idx);
   const isCaption=captionIndices.has(idx);
   body+='<p'+(isHead?' class="topic2Head"':isCaption?' class="topic2Caption"':'')+'>'+topic2Escape(txt)+'</p>';
  }
 }
 el.innerHTML='<div class="lessonTitle"><div class="eyebrow">TOPIC 2 / 主题二 / Zhǔtí èr</div><h1>Evaluating and Selecting Quality Literature</h1><p>评估与选择优质儿童文学作品</p><p> Pínggū yǔ xuǎnzé yōuzhì értóng wénxué zuòpǐn</p></div><section class="topic2Lecture">'+body+'</section><section class="topic2Quiz"><h2>Student-Facing Quiz / 学生测验 / Xuéshēng cèyàn</h2><div id="topic2QuizArea"></div></section><button class="action" type="button" onclick="completeTopic(1)">Mark topic complete / 标记主题已完成 / Biāojì zhǔtí yǐ wánchéng</button>';
 renderTopic2Quiz();
}
function renderTopic2Quiz(){
 const root=document.getElementById('topic2QuizArea');if(!root)return;
 let saved=[];try{saved=JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem('bece_topic2_quiz_answers')||'[]')}catch(e){}
 root.innerHTML=topic2Questions.map((q,i)=>'<fieldset><legend>Question '+(i+1)+'<div>'+topic2Lines(q.title)+'</div><div>'+topic2Lines(q.stem)+'</div></legend>'+q.options.map((o,j)=>'<label><input type="radio" name="topic2q'+i+'" value="'+j+'" '+(saved[i]===j?'checked':'')+' onchange="saveTopic2Answers()"> '+topic2Lines(o)+'</label>').join('')+'</fieldset>').join('')+'<button class="action" type="button" onclick="gradeTopic2Quiz()">Check answers / 检查答案 / Jiǎnchá dá’àn</button> <button class="back" type="button" onclick="resetTopic2Quiz()">Reset / 重置 / Chóngzhì</button><div id="topic2Result" role="status" aria-live="polite"></div>';
}
function topic2Answers(){return topic2Questions.map((q,i)=>{const x=document.querySelector('input[name="topic2q'+i+'"]:checked');return x?Number(x.value):null})}
function saveTopic2Answers(){localStorage.setItem('bece_topic2_quiz_answers',JSON.stringify(topic2Answers()))}
function gradeTopic2Quiz(){
 const a=topic2Answers(),answered=a.filter(x=>x!==null).length,score=a.reduce((n,v,i)=>n+(v!==null&&v===topic2Questions[i].correct?1:0),0);
 const result=document.getElementById('topic2Result');if(!result)return;
 if(!answered){result.textContent='Please answer at least one question. / 请至少回答一道题。 / Qǐng zhìshǎo huídá yí dào tí.';return}
 let out='<h3>Score: '+score+' / '+answered+' answered (10 total)</h3><p>分数：'+score+' / '+answered+'（共10题）</p>';
 topic2Questions.forEach((q,i)=>{if(a[i]===null)return;out+='<div class="topic2Feedback"><strong>Question '+(i+1)+': '+(a[i]===q.correct?'Correct / 正确':'Review / 复习')+'</strong><p>Best answer: '+ 'ABCD'[q.correct]+'</p>'+q.explanations.map((e,j)=>'<p><b>'+ 'ABCD'[j]+'.</b> '+topic2Escape(e.replace(/^[- ]*[A-D][.:]\s*/,''))+'</p>').join('')+'</div>'});
 result.innerHTML=out;
 if(answered===10){localStorage.setItem('bece_topic2_quiz_score',String(score));localStorage.setItem('bece_topic2_quiz_last_completed',new Date().toISOString())}
}
function resetTopic2Quiz(){localStorage.removeItem('bece_topic2_quiz_answers');renderTopic2Quiz()}
function renderTopic2LecturerNotes(){
 const el=document.getElementById('lecturer');if(!el||document.getElementById('topic2LecturerNotes'))return;
 const wrap=document.createElement('section');wrap.id='topic2LecturerNotes';wrap.className='card topic2Lecturer';
 wrap.innerHTML='<h2>Topic 2 — Lecturer Teaching Notes</h2><p>主题二——讲师教学笔记</p><p>For lecturer reference. This section is not part of the student quiz. Note: the current PWA does not enforce role-based access.</p><details><summary>Show / hide approved teaching notes</summary>'+topic2LecturerNotes.map(s=>{const heading=/^Question\s+\d+\s*[—–-]/.test(s);const sub=/^(Teaching point|Common misconception|Discussion prompt|Correct answer|Distractor analysis|Teaching points|Common misconceptions|Discussion prompts|Quality review note):/.test(s);return '<p'+(heading?' class="topic2NoteQuestion"':sub?' class="topic2NoteSubheading"':'')+'>'+topic2Escape(s)+'</p>'}).join('')+'</details>';
 el.appendChild(wrap)
}
renderTopic2LecturerNotes();
